{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 00:27:40", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-6c64d384-c013-40f4-a7e7-72c80ce7c1dd', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "project_id": "088a1756",\n  "project_name": "Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "implementation_spec": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/implementation_spec.md",\n  "target_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/HorizontalTimelineView.jsx",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "Implement scroll preservation during periodic data refreshes to prevent user view disruption"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AjPLT5bXvJbJVk5jBFSxZt', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AjPLT5bXvJbJVk5jBFSxZt', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix Requirements\\n\\n## User Problem\\nThe timeline page currently disrupts user focus by changing the view every time data refreshes, causing a poor user experience.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Prevent automatic scrolling/view changes during data refresh\\n2. Maintain user\'s current view/scroll position\\n3. Ensure data updates occur without visual interruption\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Preserve real-time data updates\\n- Minimal performance impact\\n- Compatible with existing timeline component\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- User\'s current view remains stable during data refresh\\n- No unexpected scrolling or repositioning\\n- Data updates occur smoothly in the background\\n- Performance overhead is negligible\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Refresh mechanism is currently tied to view reset\\n- Likely requires decoupling data refresh from view state\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI/UX redesign\\n- Changing data refresh frequency\\n- Modifying existing data fetch mechanisms\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n- Zero unexpected view shifts during data refresh\\n- User reports improved experience\\n- No introduction of new performance bottlenecks"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01APoSNcP5duRcPACWakKX5z', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/implementation_spec.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01APoSNcP5duRcPACWakKX5z', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Implementation Specification: Timeline Scroll Preservation\\n\\n## Objective\\nModify HorizontalTimelineView component to maintain user\'s scroll position during periodic data refreshes.\\n\\n## Required Changes in `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/HorizontalTimelineView.jsx`\\n\\n### 1. Import Updates\\n```javascript\\nimport React, { useState, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from \'react\';\\n```\\n\\n### 2. State and Ref Management\\n- Add new refs to track scroll position:\\n```javascript\\nconst containerRef = useRef(null);\\nconst scrollPositionRef = useRef({ x: 0, y: 0 });\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Scroll Preservation Methods\\nImplement two new methods:\\n```javascript\\nconst preserveScrollPosition = useCallback(() => {\\n  if (containerRef.current) {\\n    scrollPositionRef.current = {\\n      x: containerRef.current.scrollLeft,\\n      y: containerRef.current.scrollTop\\n    };\\n  }\\n}, []);\\n\\nconst restoreScrollPosition = useCallback(() => {\\n  if (containerRef.current) {\\n    containerRef.current.scrollLeft = scrollPositionRef.current.x;\\n    containerRef.current.scrollTop = scrollPositionRef.current.y;\\n  }\\n}, []);\\n```\\n\\n### 4. Modify `useEffect` for Request Fetching\\nUpdate to preserve scroll state:\\n```javascript\\nuseEffect(() => {\\n  const fetchRequests = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      preserveScrollPosition();\\n      const response = await fetch(\'http://localhost:8001/api/requests?limit=20\');\\n      // Existing fetch logic\\n      \\n      setTimeout(restoreScrollPosition, 0);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      // Existing error handling\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  fetchRequests();\\n  const interval = setInterval(fetchRequests, 2000);\\n  return () => clearInterval(interval);\\n}, [preserveScrollPosition, restoreScrollPosition, selectedRequest]);\\n```\\n\\n### 5. Container Ref Update\\nModify container div to use new ref:\\n```javascript\\n<div\\n  ref={containerRef}\\n  style={{\\n    flex: 1,\\n    overflowX: \'auto\',\\n    overflowY: \'auto\',\\n    padding: \'20px\'\\n  }}\\n>\\n  {/* Existing content */}\\n</div>\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Requirements\\n1. Verify scroll position remains stable during periodic refreshes\\n2. Test with long timeline and varied scroll positions\\n3. Ensure no performance degradation\\n4. Validate across different browsers\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n- Use `useCallback` to memoize scroll methods\\n- Minimal overhead with `setTimeout` for scroll restoration\\n- Preserve existing component logic\\n\\n## Browser Compatibility\\n- Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)\\n- React 17+ recommended\\n- ES6+ environment required"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Pe