{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 00:28:55", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-3309f0fe-3eae-41d0-8791-515c2b4ac644', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "project_name": "Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix",\n  "milestone": "Implement scroll preservation in HorizontalTimelineView",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "implementation_spec": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/implementation_spec.md",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01V9WKCJPMqN2bWfnqW89uyT', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01V9WKCJPMqN2bWfnqW89uyT', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix Requirements\\n\\n## User Problem\\nThe timeline page currently disrupts user focus by changing the view every time data refreshes, causing a poor user experience.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Prevent automatic scrolling/view changes during data refresh\\n2. Maintain user\'s current view/scroll position\\n3. Ensure data updates occur without visual interruption\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Preserve real-time data updates\\n- Minimal performance impact\\n- Compatible with existing timeline component\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- User\'s current view remains stable during data refresh\\n- No unexpected scrolling or repositioning\\n- Data updates occur smoothly in the background\\n- Performance overhead is negligible\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Refresh mechanism is currently tied to view reset\\n- Likely requires decoupling data refresh from view state\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI/UX redesign\\n- Changing data refresh frequency\\n- Modifying existing data fetch mechanisms\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n- Zero unexpected view shifts during data refresh\\n- User reports improved experience\\n- No introduction of new performance bottlenecks"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0185JEeyRdLQRurLToNiAP7Q', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/implementation_spec.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0185JEeyRdLQRurLToNiAP7Q', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Implementation Specification: Timeline Scroll Preservation\\n\\n## Objective\\nModify HorizontalTimelineView component to maintain user\'s scroll position during periodic data refreshes.\\n\\n## Required Changes in `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/HorizontalTimelineView.jsx`\\n\\n### 1. Import Updates\\n```javascript\\nimport React, { useState, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from \'react\';\\n```\\n\\n### 2. State and Ref Management\\n- Add new refs to track scroll position:\\n```javascript\\nconst containerRef = useRef(null);\\nconst scrollPositionRef = useRef({ x: 0, y: 0 });\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Scroll Preservation Methods\\nImplement two new methods:\\n```javascript\\nconst preserveScrollPosition = useCallback(() => {\\n  if (containerRef.current) {\\n    scrollPositionRef.current = {\\n      x: containerRef.current.scrollLeft,\\n      y: containerRef.current.scrollTop\\n    };\\n  }\\n}, []);\\n\\nconst restoreScrollPosition = useCallback(() => {\\n  if (containerRef.current) {\\n    containerRef.current.scrollLeft = scrollPositionRef.current.x;\\n    containerRef.current.scrollTop = scrollPositionRef.current.y;\\n  }\\n}, []);\\n```\\n\\n### 4. Modify `useEffect` for Request Fetching\\nUpdate to preserve scroll state:\\n```javascript\\nuseEffect(() => {\\n  const fetchRequests = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      preserveScrollPosition();\\n      const response = await fetch(\'http://localhost:8001/api/requests?limit=20\');\\n      // Existing fetch logic\\n      \\n      setTimeout(restoreScrollPosition, 0);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      // Existing error handling\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  fetchRequests();\\n  const interval = setInterval(fetchRequests, 2000);\\n  return () => clearInterval(interval);\\n}, [preserveScrollPosition, restoreScrollPosition, selectedRequest]);\\n```\\n\\n### 5. Container Ref Update\\nModify container div to use new ref:\\n```javascript\\n<div\\n  ref={containerRef}\\n  style={{\\n    flex: 1,\\n    overflowX: \'auto\',\\n    overflowY: \'auto\',\\n    padding: \'20px\'\\n  }}\\n>\\n  {/* Existing content */}\\n</div>\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Requirements\\n1. Verify scroll position remains stable during periodic refreshes\\n2. Test with long timeline and varied scroll positions\\n3. Ensure no performance degradation\\n4. Validate across different browsers\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n- Use `useCallback` to memoize scroll methods\\n- Minimal overhead with `setTimeout` for scroll restoration\\n- Preserve existing component logic\\n\\n## Browser Compatibility\\n- Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)\\n- React 17+ recommended\\n- ES6+ environment required"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01HPNgZaqjxEk9LFs3StWjPP', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01HPNgZaqjxEk9LFs3StWjPP', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis architecture proposal addresses the focus disruption issue by implementing a **State-Aware Data Refresh Pattern** that separates data management from view state management. The solution employs a React-based architecture with custom hooks and memoization strategies to ensure smooth, non-disruptive data updates.\\n\\n### Core Architectural Pattern\\n**Separation of Concerns with Controlled Re-rendering**\\n- Data refresh logic isolated from view positioning logic\\n- Selective component updates using React.memo and useMemo\\n- Scroll position preservation through custom hook management\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend Framework: React (Existing)\\n**Why**: Already in use, provides excellent state management and re-rendering control\\n**Alternatives Considered**: Vue.js (not chosen due to existing React codebase)\\n\\n### State Management: React Hooks + Context API\\n**Why**: \\n- Lightweight solution for focused scope\\n- Excellent re-rendering control\\n- Minimal overhead compared to Redux for this specific use case\\n**Alternatives Considered**: Redux (overkill for this focused fix)\\n\\n### Scroll Management: Custom React Hook\\n**Why**: Provides reusable, focused scroll position management\\n**Implementation**: useScrollPosition hook with throttling\\n\\n### Performance Optimization: React.memo + useMemo\\n**Why**: Prevents unnecessary re-renders during data updates\\n**Implementation**: Selective memoization of timeline components\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. ViewStateManager (Custom Hook)\\n**Responsibility**: Preserve and restore scroll position and view state\\n```\\nuseViewState() -> {\\n  scrollPosition: number,\\n  preservePosition: () => void,\\n  restorePosition: () => void\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 2. DataRefreshController (Custom Hook)\\n**Responsibility**: Manage data refresh without triggering view changes\\n```\\nuseDataRefresh() -> {\\n  refreshData: () => void,\\n  isRefreshing: boolean,\\n  lastUpdate: timestamp\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 3. TimelineContainer (Component)\\n**Responsibility**: Coordinate between data and view state\\n**Key Features**:\\n- Wraps existing timeline component\\n- Implements view state preservation\\n- Controls re-rendering scope\\n\\n### 4. MemoizedTimelineItems (Component)\\n**Responsibility**: Render timeline items with selective updates\\n**Key Features**:\\n- React.memo wrapper for performance\\n- Stable key generation for items\\n- Conditional re-rendering based on data changes\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n```\\nUser Interaction -> ViewState Preserved\\n                     \\u2193\\nData Refresh Triggered -> DataRefreshController\\n                     \\u2193\\nNew Data Received -> Selective Component Updates\\n                     \\u2193\\nView State Restored -> User Experience Maintained\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 timeline/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TimelineContainer.jsx          # Main container component\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MemoizedTimelineItems.jsx      # Optimized timeline items\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502           \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TimelineContainer.test.js\\n\\u2502           \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 integration.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useViewState.js                    # Scroll position management\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useDataRefresh.js                  # Data refresh control\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useViewState.test.js\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useDataRefresh.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 scrollUtils.js                     # Scroll position utilities\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 constants/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 refreshConstants.js                # Configuration constants\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### ViewState Interface\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  scrollTop: number,\\n  scrollLeft: number,\\n  focusedItemId: string | null,\\n  timestamp: number\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### RefreshState Interface\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  isRefreshing: boolean,\\n  lastRefresh: Date,\\n  refreshCount: number,\\n  preserveView: boolean\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## API Integration\\n\\n### Existing Timeline API (Preserved)\\n- No changes to existing data fetch endpoints\\n- Maintains current real-time update mechanisms\\n- Preserves existing authentication and error handling\\n\\n### New Internal APIs\\n```javascript\\n// ViewState Management\\nviewStateManager.preserve()\\nviewStateManager.restore()\\nviewStateManager.getSnapshot()\\n\\n// Data Refresh Control\\ndataRefreshController.refreshWithViewPreservation()\\ndataRefreshController.setRefreshMode(mode)\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation Strategy\\n\\n### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (2-3 days)\\n1. Create custom hooks (useViewState, useDataRefresh)\\n2. Implement scroll position utilities\\n3. Add basic test coverage\\n\\n### Phase 2: Component Integration (2-3 days)\\n1. Create TimelineContainer wrapper\\n2. Implement MemoizedTimelineItems\\n3. Integrate with existing timeline component\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing & Refinement (2-3 days)\\n1. Comprehensive testing across browsers\\n2. Performance optimization\\n3. Edge case handling\\n\\n### Deployment Strategy\\n**Incremental Rollout**:\\n1. Feature flag implementation for A/B testing\\n2. Gradual rollout to user segments\\n3. Performance monitoring and rollback capability\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- **Hooks Testing**: Custom hooks isolated testing with React Testing Library\\n- **Component Testing**: TimelineContainer and MemoizedTimelineItems\\n- **Utility Testing**: Scroll position calculation and preservation\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- **End-to-End Scenarios**: Full data refresh cycle with view preservation\\n- **Performance Testing**: Memory usage and re-render frequency\\n- **Cross-Browser Testing**: Scroll behavior consistency\\n\\n### Test Implementation\\n```javascript\\n// Example test structure\\ndescribe(\'ViewState Preservation\', () => {\\n  test(\'maintains scroll position during data refresh\', () => {\\n    // Test scroll position before/after refresh\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'prevents unexpected view jumps\', () => {\\n    // Test for view stability\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n\\n### Optimization Strategies\\n1. **Throttled Scroll Tracking**: Limit scroll position updates to 16ms intervals\\n2. **Selective Memoization**: Only memoize components that benefit from it\\n3. **Debounced Refresh**: Prevent rapid successive refresh calls\\n\\n### Memory Management\\n- Cleanup scroll listeners on component unmount\\n- Limit view state history to prevent memory leaks\\n- Use WeakMap for component-specific state storage\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### 1. Complete Timeline Component Rewrite\\n**Pros**: Clean slate approach, optimal performance\\n**Cons**: High risk, significant development time, potential for new bugs\\n**Decision**: Rejected due to scope constraints and risk\\n\\n### 2. Third-Party Scroll Management Library\\n**Pros**: Proven solution, extensive features\\n**Cons**: Additional dependency, potential overkill, bundle size increase\\n**Decision**: Rejected in favor of lightweight custom solution\\n\\n### 3. CSS-Only Solution\\n**Pros**: No JavaScript overhead, simple implementation\\n**Cons**: Limited control, browser compatibility issues\\n**Decision**: Rejected due to insufficient control over dynamic content\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Performance Degradation\\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive performance testing, selective optimization\\n**Monitoring**: React DevTools profiling, lighthouse audits\\n\\n### Risk 2: Browser Compatibility\\n**Mitigation**: Cross-browser testing, progressive enhancement\\n**Fallback**: Graceful degradation to current behavior\\n\\n### Risk 3: Complex Edge Cases\\n**Mitigation**: Incremental rollout, extensive testing\\n**Strategy**: Feature flags for quick rollback if issues arise\\n\\n### Risk 4: Integration Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**: Minimal changes to existing components, wrapper-based approach\\n**Testing**: Isolated testing environment, staging deployment\\n\\n## Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. **Performance vs. Smoothness Trade-off**: Should we prioritize absolute minimal performance impact or smoothest user experience?\\n\\n2. **Fallback Strategy**: In case of scroll position restoration failure, should we maintain current position or reset to top?\\n\\n3. **Feature Flag Duration**: How long should the A/B testing period be before full rollout?\\n\\n4. **Refresh Frequency Impact**: Should this solution influence the current data refresh frequency, or maintain it exactly as-is?\\n\\n## Success Metrics & Monitoring\\n\\n### Primary Metrics\\n- **View Stability**: Zero unexpected scroll jumps during refresh (target: 100%)\\n- **User Experience**: Reduced user complaints about focus disruption\\n- **Performance**: No increase in render time (target: <5ms overhead)\\n\\n### Monitoring Implementation\\n- Custom analytics events for view preservation success/failure\\n- Performance monitoring integration\\n- User feedback collection mechanism\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a surgical solution to the focus disruption problem while maintaining compatibility with existing systems. The separation of concerns approach ensures maintainability, and the incremental implementation strategy minimizes risk while delivering measurable user experience improvements."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Frontend Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nBreaks frontend milestones into specific component, page, and service tasks. Analyzes architecture and requirements to identify UI components, user flows, state management, and API integration needs. Coordinates frontend development through TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou break frontend work into actionable tasks for TDD Coordinator to implement via TDD.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable UI/UX assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\nSee [Common Instructions - Default Assumptions](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#default-assumptions) for standard technical defaults.\n\n**Frontend-Specific Defaults** (use unless architecture specifies otherwise):\n**Framework**: React with hooks or Vue 3 with Composition API\n**Styling**: Tailwind CSS or CSS Modules\n**State**: Context API (simple) or Redux/Vuex (complex)\n**API Client**: fetch or axios with error handling\n**Forms**: Controlled components with validation\n**Routing**: React Router or Vue Router\n**Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify all frontend components:\n  * Pages/Routes\n  * UI components (forms, buttons, cards, modals)\n  * Services (API client, WebSocket, auth)\n  * State management (Context, Redux, stores)\n  * Utilities (formatting, validation)\n  * Styling (CSS, Tailwind classes)\n\n**2. Break Down Into Tasks**\nFor each component, create specific tasks:\nTask name (concise, actionable)\nDescription (what needs to be built)\nAcceptance criteria (user can do X, component shows Y)\nDependencies (what must exist first)\nEstimated complexity (simple|medium|complex)\n\n**3. Organize by User Flow**\nGroup by user journey or feature\nOrder by dependencies (layout → components → pages)\nIdentify reusable components\n\n**4. Write Task Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Frontend Tasks - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to break down",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "tasks_identified": "integer - number of tasks created",\n  "task_file": "string - path to task breakdown document",\n  "dependencies": "array - list of task dependencies",\n  "message": "string - summary of task breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **User flow is genuinely ambiguous** (e.g., "manage users" without specifying CRUD operations)\n- **Multiple valid UX approaches with major trade-offs** (e.g., modal vs full-page form)\n- **Design requirements are contradictory** (e.g., "simple but feature-rich")\n- **Accessibility requirements unclear** (e.g., WCAG level needed)\n- **NOT for**: standard UI patterns, common component structures, typical interactions\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All frontend tasks identified and documented\n- Component hierarchy mapped\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 98.4%\n- Average iterations per task: 4.2\n- Common errors to avoid: BadRequestError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: BadRequestError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 