{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 00:29:28", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-656c5027-7083-4077-9ce1-a5e14cca5d87', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "project_name": "Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix",\n  "milestone": "Test scroll preservation in HorizontalTimelineView",\n  "requirements": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "architecture": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XPtxQufBvoQ5Zpam47CfhR', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XPtxQufBvoQ5Zpam47CfhR', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix Requirements\\n\\n## User Problem\\nThe timeline page currently disrupts user focus by changing the view every time data refreshes, causing a poor user experience.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Prevent automatic scrolling/view changes during data refresh\\n2. Maintain user\'s current view/scroll position\\n3. Ensure data updates occur without visual interruption\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Preserve real-time data updates\\n- Minimal performance impact\\n- Compatible with existing timeline component\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- User\'s current view remains stable during data refresh\\n- No unexpected scrolling or repositioning\\n- Data updates occur smoothly in the background\\n- Performance overhead is negligible\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Refresh mechanism is currently tied to view reset\\n- Likely requires decoupling data refresh from view state\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI/UX redesign\\n- Changing data refresh frequency\\n- Modifying existing data fetch mechanisms\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n- Zero unexpected view shifts during data refresh\\n- User reports improved experience\\n- No introduction of new performance bottlenecks"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XC3MRMqA7Svk8oHfij8RRQ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XC3MRMqA7Svk8oHfij8RRQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis architecture proposal addresses the focus disruption issue by implementing a **State-Aware Data Refresh Pattern** that separates data management from view state management. The solution employs a React-based architecture with custom hooks and memoization strategies to ensure smooth, non-disruptive data updates.\\n\\n### Core Architectural Pattern\\n**Separation of Concerns with Controlled Re-rendering**\\n- Data refresh logic isolated from view positioning logic\\n- Selective component updates using React.memo and useMemo\\n- Scroll position preservation through custom hook management\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend Framework: React (Existing)\\n**Why**: Already in use, provides excellent state management and re-rendering control\\n**Alternatives Considered**: Vue.js (not chosen due to existing React codebase)\\n\\n### State Management: React Hooks + Context API\\n**Why**: \\n- Lightweight solution for focused scope\\n- Excellent re-rendering control\\n- Minimal overhead compared to Redux for this specific use case\\n**Alternatives Considered**: Redux (overkill for this focused fix)\\n\\n### Scroll Management: Custom React Hook\\n**Why**: Provides reusable, focused scroll position management\\n**Implementation**: useScrollPosition hook with throttling\\n\\n### Performance Optimization: React.memo + useMemo\\n**Why**: Prevents unnecessary re-renders during data updates\\n**Implementation**: Selective memoization of timeline components\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. ViewStateManager (Custom Hook)\\n**Responsibility**: Preserve and restore scroll position and view state\\n```\\nuseViewState() -> {\\n  scrollPosition: number,\\n  preservePosition: () => void,\\n  restorePosition: () => void\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 2. DataRefreshController (Custom Hook)\\n**Responsibility**: Manage data refresh without triggering view changes\\n```\\nuseDataRefresh() -> {\\n  refreshData: () => void,\\n  isRefreshing: boolean,\\n  lastUpdate: timestamp\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 3. TimelineContainer (Component)\\n**Responsibility**: Coordinate between data and view state\\n**Key Features**:\\n- Wraps existing timeline component\\n- Implements view state preservation\\n- Controls re-rendering scope\\n\\n### 4. MemoizedTimelineItems (Component)\\n**Responsibility**: Render timeline items with selective updates\\n**Key Features**:\\n- React.memo wrapper for performance\\n- Stable key generation for items\\n- Conditional re-rendering based on data changes\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n```\\nUser Interaction -> ViewState Preserved\\n                     \\u2193\\nData Refresh Triggered -> DataRefreshController\\n                     \\u2193\\nNew Data Received -> Selective Component Updates\\n                     \\u2193\\nView State Restored -> User Experience Maintained\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 timeline/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TimelineContainer.jsx          # Main container component\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MemoizedTimelineItems.jsx      # Optimized timeline items\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502           \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TimelineContainer.test.js\\n\\u2502           \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 integration.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useViewState.js                    # Scroll position management\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useDataRefresh.js                  # Data refresh control\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useViewState.test.js\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useDataRefresh.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 scrollUtils.js                     # Scroll position utilities\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 constants/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 refreshConstants.js                # Configuration constants\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### ViewState Interface\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  scrollTop: number,\\n  scrollLeft: number,\\n  focusedItemId: string | null,\\n  timestamp: number\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### RefreshState Interface\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  isRefreshing: boolean,\\n  lastRefresh: Date,\\n  refreshCount: number,\\n  preserveView: boolean\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## API Integration\\n\\n### Existing Timeline API (Preserved)\\n- No changes to existing data fetch endpoints\\n- Maintains current real-time update mechanisms\\n- Preserves existing authentication and error handling\\n\\n### New Internal APIs\\n```javascript\\n// ViewState Management\\nviewStateManager.preserve()\\nviewStateManager.restore()\\nviewStateManager.getSnapshot()\\n\\n// Data Refresh Control\\ndataRefreshController.refreshWithViewPreservation()\\ndataRefreshController.setRefreshMode(mode)\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation Strategy\\n\\n### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (2-3 days)\\n1. Create custom hooks (useViewState, useDataRefresh)\\n2. Implement scroll position utilities\\n3. Add basic test coverage\\n\\n### Phase 2: Component Integration (2-3 days)\\n1. Create TimelineContainer wrapper\\n2. Implement MemoizedTimelineItems\\n3. Integrate with existing timeline component\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing & Refinement (2-3 days)\\n1. Comprehensive testing across browsers\\n2. Performance optimization\\n3. Edge case handling\\n\\n### Deployment Strategy\\n**Incremental Rollout**:\\n1. Feature flag implementation for A/B testing\\n2. Gradual rollout to user segments\\n3. Performance monitoring and rollback capability\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- **Hooks Testing**: Custom hooks isolated testing with React Testing Library\\n- **Component Testing**: TimelineContainer and MemoizedTimelineItems\\n- **Utility Testing**: Scroll position calculation and preservation\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- **End-to-End Scenarios**: Full data refresh cycle with view preservation\\n- **Performance Testing**: Memory usage and re-render frequency\\n- **Cross-Browser Testing**: Scroll behavior consistency\\n\\n### Test Implementation\\n```javascript\\n// Example test structure\\ndescribe(\'ViewState Preservation\', () => {\\n  test(\'maintains scroll position during data refresh\', () => {\\n    // Test scroll position before/after refresh\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'prevents unexpected view jumps\', () => {\\n    // Test for view stability\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n\\n### Optimization Strategies\\n1. **Throttled Scroll Tracking**: Limit scroll position updates to 16ms intervals\\n2. **Selective Memoization**: Only memoize components that benefit from it\\n3. **Debounced Refresh**: Prevent rapid successive refresh calls\\n\\n### Memory Management\\n- Cleanup scroll listeners on component unmount\\n- Limit view state history to prevent memory leaks\\n- Use WeakMap for component-specific state storage\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### 1. Complete Timeline Component Rewrite\\n**Pros**: Clean slate approach, optimal performance\\n**Cons**: High risk, significant development time, potential for new bugs\\n**Decision**: Rejected due to scope constraints and risk\\n\\n### 2. Third-Party Scroll Management Library\\n**Pros**: Proven solution, extensive features\\n**Cons**: Additional dependency, potential overkill, bundle size increase\\n**Decision**: Rejected in favor of lightweight custom solution\\n\\n### 3. CSS-Only Solution\\n**Pros**: No JavaScript overhead, simple implementation\\n**Cons**: Limited control, browser compatibility issues\\n**Decision**: Rejected due to insufficient control over dynamic content\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Performance Degradation\\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive performance testing, selective optimization\\n**Monitoring**: React DevTools profiling, lighthouse audits\\n\\n### Risk 2: Browser Compatibility\\n**Mitigation**: Cross-browser testing, progressive enhancement\\n**Fallback**: Graceful degradation to current behavior\\n\\n### Risk 3: Complex Edge Cases\\n**Mitigation**: Incremental rollout, extensive testing\\n**Strategy**: Feature flags for quick rollback if issues arise\\n\\n### Risk 4: Integration Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**: Minimal changes to existing components, wrapper-based approach\\n**Testing**: Isolated testing environment, staging deployment\\n\\n## Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. **Performance vs. Smoothness Trade-off**: Should we prioritize absolute minimal performance impact or smoothest user experience?\\n\\n2. **Fallback Strategy**: In case of scroll position restoration failure, should we maintain current position or reset to top?\\n\\n3. **Feature Flag Duration**: How long should the A/B testing period be before full rollout?\\n\\n4. **Refresh Frequency Impact**: Should this solution influence the current data refresh frequency, or maintain it exactly as-is?\\n\\n## Success Metrics & Monitoring\\n\\n### Primary Metrics\\n- **View Stability**: Zero unexpected scroll jumps during refresh (target: 100%)\\n- **User Experience**: Reduced user complaints about focus disruption\\n- **Performance**: No increase in render time (target: <5ms overhead)\\n\\n### Monitoring Implementation\\n- Custom analytics events for view preservation success/failure\\n- Performance monitoring integration\\n- User feedback collection mechanism\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a surgical solution to the focus disruption problem while maintaining compatibility with existing systems. The separation of concerns approach ensures maintainability, and the incremental implementation strategy minimizes risk while delivering measurable user experience improvements."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01WbSsoyMapFvhUWCbswJdxV', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Testing', 'description': 'Comprehensive test strategy for scroll preservation in HorizontalTimelineView'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01WbSsoyMapFvhUWCbswJdxV', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "90b2edcc", "message": "Created project: Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Testing", "summary": {"project_id": "90b2edcc", "project_name": "Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Testing", "description": "Comprehensive test strategy for scroll preservation in HorizontalTimelineView", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-17T00:29:28.621242", "updated_at": "2026-01-17T00:29:28.621242", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-17T00:29:28.621242", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Testing\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 97.8%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.9\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
