lementation of Achievement Audit and Cleanup milestone with TDD approach", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "34 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "46626a3b770fb56781a8af825cf8a158764b5350", "message": "Milestone 1 implementation begin: Prepared directories, spawned coordinators, and initiated TDD process for Achievement Consolidation", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "35 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "3bd28764e6f06fc8c986a4320410f7828dc12bc0", "message": "Milestone 1 planning for Achievement Consolidation: Finalized architecture, milestone plan, and task breakdowns for backend and testing", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "37 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "8051fe315ddd7ca04ebf7c55f477044c2cdc5981", "message": "Add requirements for achievement system consolidation and expansion", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "39 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "f57958ab035753c52bf7a1402397e2e762bcb061", "message": "Complete Milestone 1 setup: API Cost Optimization research and documentation phase initiated", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "7e54be9371ee12a85485c76535564da32a2e0fe3", "message": "Initial project setup for Tmux Monitoring Dashboard", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "f5c30d44529777f9401b64f6a436c04296771d2d", "message": "Complete Milestone 3: Full CLI Integration and Polish for Tmux Monitoring Dashboard", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "0b91cf675d9906a8b0d3971d312bc2549ffe1100", "message": "Complete Milestone 3: Full CLI Integration and Polish for Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - implemented Claude CLI integration, advanced log processing, configuration management system, robust error handling, and cross-platform compatibility features", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "017db01e1eedbe015d976d87c4730760912bd86f", "message": "Complete Milestone 2 Integration and Testing: comprehensive testing achieved with 95% coverage and sub-millisecond performance", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "476015b52cdfb1c8c2660e0bbaa7fbf0e548e992", "message": "Complete Milestone 2: Enhanced Task Monitoring with real-time tracking", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "7f7ce8b59169360f3b44a54332e854f54acb860c", "message": "Complete TDD Coordinator model validation with comprehensive performance report", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "80509b30d6cd7a13eaa6c9d5f9cfcf3668dedf9a", "message": "Complete backend implementation and testing for TDD Coordinator model validation A/B testing framework", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "b72edcd8bdc67384c51b097bf4f11919bcaff5c8", "message": "Complete Milestone 1: Basic Tmux Layout for Monitoring Dashboard", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "24e4cfbfe17daa33a6ee682dee447d88770e5f8d", "message": "Complete milestone 3: final deployment preparation for activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "282711affb101f9a14d654eb0691b7ed2cade355", "message": "Prepare final deployment package for activity tracking system with comprehensive requirements and deployment instructions", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "1ca876e0c7da20a2ba22cb1eddc5b81ab6786156", "message": "Complete milestone 2: comprehensive integration testing for activity tracking system", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}, {"hash": "db7897db012286d819174b33609ec1e9edd6bbe4", "message": "Complete implementation milestone: Loser Board feature with backend, frontend, and test suite", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "2 hours ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011oUa14KsDxq3Grf3jnFfaJ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011oUa14KsDxq3Grf3jnFfaJ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix Requirements\\n\\n## User Problem\\nThe timeline page currently disrupts user focus by changing the view every time data refreshes, causing a poor user experience.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Prevent automatic scrolling/view changes during data refresh\\n2. Maintain user\'s current view/scroll position\\n3. Ensure data updates occur without visual interruption\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Preserve real-time data updates\\n- Minimal performance impact\\n- Compatible with existing timeline component\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- User\'s current view remains stable during data refresh\\n- No unexpected scrolling or repositioning\\n- Data updates occur smoothly in the background\\n- Performance overhead is negligible\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Refresh mechanism is currently tied to view reset\\n- Likely requires decoupling data refresh from view state\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI/UX redesign\\n- Changing data refresh frequency\\n- Modifying existing data fetch mechanisms\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n- Zero unexpected view shifts during data refresh\\n- User reports improved experience\\n- No introduction of new performance bottlenecks"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CVFSybZFoHxb7E5idJQSyi', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CVFSybZFoHxb7E5idJQSyi', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis architecture proposal addresses the focus disruption issue by implementing a **State-Aware Data Refresh Pattern** that separates data management from view state management. The solution employs a React-based architecture with custom hooks and memoization strategies to ensure smooth, non-disruptive data updates.\\n\\n### Core Architectural Pattern\\n**Separation of Concerns with Controlled Re-rendering**\\n- Data refresh logic isolated from view positioning logic\\n- Selective component updates using React.memo and useMemo\\n- Scroll position preservation through custom hook management\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend Framework: React (Existing)\\n**Why**: Already in use, provides excellent state management and re-rendering control\\n**Alternatives Considered**: Vue.js (not chosen due to existing React codebase)\\n\\n### State Management: React Hooks + Context API\\n**Why**: \\n- Lightweight solution for focused scope\\n- Excellent re-rendering control\\n- Minimal overhead compared to Redux for this specific use case\\n**Alternatives Considered**: Redux (overkill for this focused fix)\\n\\n### Scroll Management: Custom React Hook\\n**Why**: Provides reusable, focused scroll position management\\n**Implementation**: useScrollPosition hook with throttling\\n\\n### Performance Optimization: React.memo + useMemo\\n**Why**: Prevents unnecessary re-renders during data updates\\n**Implementation**: Selective memoization of timeline components\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. ViewStateManager (Custom Hook)\\n**Responsibility**: Preserve and restore scroll position and view state\\n```\\nuseViewState() -> {\\n  scrollPosition: number,\\n  preservePosition: () => void,\\n  restorePosition: () => void\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 2. DataRefreshController (Custom Hook)\\n**Responsibility**: Manage data refresh without triggering view changes\\n```\\nuseDataRefresh() -> {\\n  refreshData: () => void,\\n  isRefreshing: boolean,\\n  lastUpdate: timestamp\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 3. TimelineContainer (Component)\\n**Responsibility**: Coordinate between data and view state\\n**Key Features**:\\n- Wraps existing timeline component\\n- Implements view state preservation\\n- Controls re-rendering scope\\n\\n### 4. MemoizedTimelineItems (Component)\\n**Responsibility**: Render timeline items with selective updates\\n**Key Features**:\\n- React.memo wrapper for performance\\n- Stable key generation for items\\n- Conditional re-rendering based on data changes\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n```\\nUser Interaction -> ViewState Preserved\\n                     \\u2193\\nData Refresh Triggered -> DataRefreshController\\n                     \\u2193\\nNew Data Received -> Selective Component Updates\\n                     \\u2193\\nView State Restored -> User Experience Maintained\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 timeline/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TimelineContainer.jsx          # Main container component\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MemoizedTimelineItems.jsx      # Optimized timeline items\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502           \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TimelineContainer.test.js\\n\\u2502           \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 integration.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useViewState.js                    # Scroll position management\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useDataRefresh.js                  # Data refresh control\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useViewState.test.js\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useDataRefresh.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 scrollUtils.js                     # Scroll position utilities\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 constants/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 refreshConstants.js                # Configuration constants\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### ViewState Interface\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  scrollTop: number,\\n  scrollLeft: number,\\n  focusedItemId: string | null,\\n  timestamp: number\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### RefreshState Interface\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  isRefreshing: boolean,\\n  lastRefresh: Date,\\n  refreshCount: number,\\n  preserveView: boolean\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## API Integration\\n\\n### Existing Timeline API (Preserved)\\n- No changes to existing data fetch endpoints\\n- Maintains current real-time update mechanisms\\n- Preserves existing authentication and error handling\\n\\n### New Internal APIs\\n```javascript\\n// ViewState Management\\nviewStateManager.preserve()\\nviewStateManager.restore()\\nviewStateManager.getSnapshot()\\n\\n// Data Refresh Control\\ndataRefreshController.refreshWithViewPreservation()\\ndataRefreshController.setRefreshMode(mode)\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation Strategy\\n\\n### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (2-3 days)\\n1. Create custom hooks (useViewState, useDataRefresh)\\n2. Implement scroll position utilities\\n3. Add basic test coverage\\n\\n### Phase 2: Component Integration (2-3 days)\\n1. Create TimelineContainer wrapper\\n2. Implement MemoizedTimelineItems\\n3. Integrate with existing timeline component\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing & Refinement (2-3 days)\\n1. Comprehensive testing across browsers\\n2. Performance optimization\\n3. Edge case handling\\n\\n### Deployment Strategy\\n**Incremental Rollout**:\\n1. Feature flag implementation for A/B testing\\n2. Gradual rollout to user segments\\n3. Performance monitoring and rollback capability\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- **Hooks Testing**: Custom hooks isolated testing with React Testing Library\\n- **Component Testing**: TimelineContainer and MemoizedTimelineItems\\n- **Utility Testing**: Scroll position calculation and preservation\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- **End-to-End Scenarios**: Full data refresh cycle with view preservation\\n- **Performance Testing**: Memory usage and re-render frequency\\n- **Cross-Browser Testing**: Scroll behavior consistency\\n\\n### Test Implementation\\n```javascript\\n// Example test structure\\ndescribe(\'ViewState Preservation\', () => {\\n  test(\'maintains scroll position during data refresh\', () => {\\n    // Test scroll position before/after refresh\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'prevents unexpected view jumps\', () => {\\n    // Test for view stability\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n\\n### Optimization Strategies\\n1. **Throttled Scroll Tracking**: Limit scroll position updates to 16ms intervals\\n2. **Selective Memoization**: Only memoize components that benefit from it\\n3. **Debounced Refresh**: Prevent rapid successive refresh calls\\n\\n### Memory Management\\n- Cleanup scroll listeners on component unmount\\n- Limit view state history to prevent memory leaks\\n- Use WeakMap for component-specific state storage\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### 1. Complete Timeline Component Rewrite\\n**Pros**: Clean slate approach, optimal performance\\n**Cons**: High risk, significant development time, potential for new bugs\\n**Decision**: Rejected due to scope constraints and risk\\n\\n### 2. Third-Party Scroll Management Library\\n**Pros**: Proven solution, extensive features\\n**Cons**: Additional dependency, potential overkill, bundle size increase\\n**Decision**: Rejected in favor of lightweight custom solution\\n\\n### 3. CSS-Only Solution\\n**Pros**: No JavaScript overhead, simple implementation\\n**Cons**: Limited control, browser compatibility issues\\n**Decision**: Rejected due to insufficient control over dynamic content\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Performance Degradation\\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive performance testing, selective optimization\\n**Monitoring**: React DevTools profiling, lighthouse audits\\n\\n### Risk 2: Browser Compatibility\\n**Mitigation**: Cross-browser testing, progressive enhancement\\n**Fallback**: Graceful degradation to current behavior\\n\\n### Risk 3: Complex Edge Cases\\n**Mitigation**: Incremental rollout, extensive testing\\n**Strategy**: Feature flags for quick rollback if issues arise\\n\\n### Risk 4: Integration Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**: Minimal changes to existing components, wrapper-based approach\\n**Testing**: Isolated testing environment, staging deployment\\n\\n## Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. **Performance vs. Smoothness Trade-off**: Should we prioritize absolute minimal performance impact or smoothest user experience?\\n\\n2. **Fallback Strategy**: In case of scroll position restoration failure, should we maintain current position or reset to top?\\n\\n3. **Feature Flag Duration**: How long should the A/B testing period be before full rollout?\\n\\n4. **Refresh Frequency Impact**: Should this solution influence the current data refresh frequency, or maintain it exactly as-is?\\n\\n## Success Metrics & Monitoring\\n\\n### Primary Metrics\\n- **View Stability**: Zero unexpected scroll jumps during refresh (target: 100%)\\n- **User Experience**: Reduced user complaints about focus disruption\\n- **Performance**: No increase in render time (target: <5ms overhead)\\n\\n### Monitoring Implementation\\n- Custom analytics events for view preservation success/failure\\n- Performance monitoring integration\\n- User feedback collection mechanism\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a surgical solution to the focus disruption problem while maintaining compatibility with existing systems. The separation of concerns approach ensures maintainability, and the incremental implementation strategy minimizes risk while delivering measurable user experience improvements."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01AxJfNcfKA6sDTj15kNmJ3w', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01AxJfNcfKA6sDTj15kNmJ3w', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nFix the timeline page data refresh issue that disrupts user focus by changing the view every time data refreshes. Maintain user\'s current view/scroll position while ensuring real-time data updates occur without visual interruption.\\n\\n## Milestone Breakdown\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Investigation & Architecture (Week 1)\\n**Objective**: Analyze current implementation and design solution architecture\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- Current code analysis document\\n- Root cause identification \\n- Technical architecture for fix\\n- Implementation plan\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Understanding of why data refresh triggers view changes\\n- Clear technical approach identified\\n- Architecture approved for implementation\\n- No breaking changes to existing API\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Core Fix Implementation (Week 2)\\n**Objective**: Implement the core fix to decouple data refresh from view state\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- Modified timeline component with preserved view state\\n- Data refresh mechanism that doesn\'t affect scroll position\\n- Unit tests for new functionality\\n- Integration tests\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Data refreshes without changing user\'s view position\\n- All existing functionality preserved\\n- Tests pass with 100% coverage on new code\\n- No performance regression\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Testing & Polish (Week 3)\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing and user experience validation\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- End-to-end tests covering all refresh scenarios\\n- Performance benchmarks\\n- User acceptance testing results\\n- Documentation updates\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Zero view shifts during data refresh in all test scenarios\\n- Performance overhead < 5ms per refresh\\n- User testing shows improved experience\\n- Documentation updated\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 complete\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n- **Low Risk**: Well-defined problem with clear scope\\n- **Technical Risk**: Potential coupling between data and view layers\\n- **Mitigation**: Thorough analysis phase before implementation\\n\\n## Timeline\\n- **Total Duration**: 3 weeks\\n- **Resource Requirements**: Frontend developer, testing resources\\n- **Critical Path**: Investigation \\u2192 Implementation \\u2192 Testing\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n- Zero unexpected view shifts during data refresh\\n- User reports improved experience  \\n- No introduction of new performance bottlenecks\\n- 100% test coverage on modified components"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01FNfNEDnP8ZVrimMTeMvhmB', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Timeline Data Refresh Focus Fix - Continuation', 'description': 'Continuation: Fix timeline page data refresh issue that disrupts user focus by changing view every time data refreshes. Analyze existing work and complete remaining tasks.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01FNfNEDnP8ZVrimMTeMvhmB', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "ae8d6a4b", "message": "Created project: Timeline Data Refresh Focus Fix - Continuation", "summary": {"project_id": "ae8d6a4b", "project_name": "Timeline Data Refresh Focus Fix - Continuation", "description": "Continuation: Fix timeline page data refresh issue that disrupts user focus by changing view every time data refreshes. Analyze existing work and complete remaining tasks.", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-17T00:48:30.863173", "updated_at": "2026-01-17T00:48:30.863173", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-17T00:48:30.863173", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Timeline Data Refresh Focus Fix - Continuation\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01JsLtyDKVDvKGwyz1N3j86F', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'ae8d6a4b', 'category': 'general', 'note': 'Continuation session detected: Previous work includes requirements.md, architecture.md, and milestone_plan.md completed. Git history shows recent commits for timeline refresh preservation. Analyzing existing implementation to identify remaining tasks.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01JsLtyDKVDvKGwyz1N3j86F', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_016wRCWkcXqS4xTAyBajsZia', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_016wRCWkcXqS4xTAyBajsZia', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "[Errno 21] Is a directory: \'/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components\'"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo