{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 00:49:34", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-fe49c7bb-154e-47b0-b380-571d334ec35e', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Timeline Data Refresh Focus Fix - Continuation"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MRHDMX28v1VtnFM491bRqh', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MRHDMX28v1VtnFM491bRqh', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix Requirements\\n\\n## User Problem\\nThe timeline page currently disrupts user focus by changing the view every time data refreshes, causing a poor user experience.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Prevent automatic scrolling/view changes during data refresh\\n2. Maintain user\'s current view/scroll position\\n3. Ensure data updates occur without visual interruption\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- Preserve real-time data updates\\n- Minimal performance impact\\n- Compatible with existing timeline component\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n- User\'s current view remains stable during data refresh\\n- No unexpected scrolling or repositioning\\n- Data updates occur smoothly in the background\\n- Performance overhead is negligible\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Refresh mechanism is currently tied to view reset\\n- Likely requires decoupling data refresh from view state\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI/UX redesign\\n- Changing data refresh frequency\\n- Modifying existing data fetch mechanisms\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n- Zero unexpected view shifts during data refresh\\n- User reports improved experience\\n- No introduction of new performance bottlenecks"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_018fFv9UsAUcVXkLyCfw5stx', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_018fFv9UsAUcVXkLyCfw5stx', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "tmux_monitoring_dashboard_implementation", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.4", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/main.py", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/App.jsx", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AchievementsDashboard.jsx", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AgentStats.jsx", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/CostTrackingDashboard.jsx", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/MetricsDashboard.jsx", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/ProjectsDashboard.jsx", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/services/api.js", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/runtime/agents/achievements.py", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/AgentStatsDashboard.jsx"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "272ee86ee685939818be6eedc2a3797b595bfee7", "message": "Add implementation specification for timeline scroll preservation", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "22 minutes ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "272ee86ee685939818be6eedc2a3797b595bfee7", "message": "Add implementation specification for timeline scroll preservation", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "22 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "350cf394895d0146ab17c7af034d98261e77b5e0", "message": "Add timeline refresh preservation strategy document", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "23 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "5e8c78dd8d664f837a962548a2be0c34355f9e59", "message": "Complete milestone planning and architecture for Timeline Data Refresh Focus Fix - milestone 1 ready for implementation", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "26 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "8bb4a6d47bf91f105bb6ce999c64ff3b353d3821", "message": "Begin detailed implementation of Achievement Audit and Cleanup milestone with TDD approach", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "35 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "46626a3b770fb56781a8af825cf8a158764b5350", "message": "Milestone 1 implementation begin: Prepared directories, spawned coordinators, and initiated TDD process for Achievement Consolidation", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "36 minutes ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012qHDK5y1hzXQFzz6Zsd6cn', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012qHDK5y1hzXQFzz6Zsd6cn', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Milestone Plan\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nFix the timeline page data refresh issue that disrupts user focus by changing the view every time data refreshes. Maintain user\'s current view/scroll position while ensuring real-time data updates occur without visual interruption.\\n\\n## Milestone Breakdown\\n\\n### Milestone 1: Investigation & Architecture (Week 1)\\n**Objective**: Analyze current implementation and design solution architecture\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- Current code analysis document\\n- Root cause identification \\n- Technical architecture for fix\\n- Implementation plan\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Understanding of why data refresh triggers view changes\\n- Clear technical approach identified\\n- Architecture approved for implementation\\n- No breaking changes to existing API\\n\\n**Dependencies**: None\\n\\n### Milestone 2: Core Fix Implementation (Week 2)\\n**Objective**: Implement the core fix to decouple data refresh from view state\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- Modified timeline component with preserved view state\\n- Data refresh mechanism that doesn\'t affect scroll position\\n- Unit tests for new functionality\\n- Integration tests\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Data refreshes without changing user\'s view position\\n- All existing functionality preserved\\n- Tests pass with 100% coverage on new code\\n- No performance regression\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 complete\\n\\n### Milestone 3: Testing & Polish (Week 3)\\n**Objective**: Comprehensive testing and user experience validation\\n\\n**Deliverables**:\\n- End-to-end tests covering all refresh scenarios\\n- Performance benchmarks\\n- User acceptance testing results\\n- Documentation updates\\n\\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\\n- Zero view shifts during data refresh in all test scenarios\\n- Performance overhead < 5ms per refresh\\n- User testing shows improved experience\\n- Documentation updated\\n\\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 complete\\n\\n## Risk Assessment\\n- **Low Risk**: Well-defined problem with clear scope\\n- **Technical Risk**: Potential coupling between data and view layers\\n- **Mitigation**: Thorough analysis phase before implementation\\n\\n## Timeline\\n- **Total Duration**: 3 weeks\\n- **Resource Requirements**: Frontend developer, testing resources\\n- **Critical Path**: Investigation \\u2192 Implementation \\u2192 Testing\\n\\n## Success Metrics\\n- Zero unexpected view shifts during data refresh\\n- User reports improved experience  \\n- No introduction of new performance bottlenecks\\n- 100% test coverage on modified components"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01464tAAxRuUatTrcuVVNcGP', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01464tAAxRuUatTrcuVVNcGP', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\nThis architecture proposal addresses the focus disruption issue by implementing a **State-Aware Data Refresh Pattern** that separates data management from view state management. The solution employs a React-based architecture with custom hooks and memoization strategies to ensure smooth, non-disruptive data updates.\\n\\n### Core Architectural Pattern\\n**Separation of Concerns with Controlled Re-rendering**\\n- Data refresh logic isolated from view positioning logic\\n- Selective component updates using React.memo and useMemo\\n- Scroll position preservation through custom hook management\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend Framework: React (Existing)\\n**Why**: Already in use, provides excellent state management and re-rendering control\\n**Alternatives Considered**: Vue.js (not chosen due to existing React codebase)\\n\\n### State Management: React Hooks + Context API\\n**Why**: \\n- Lightweight solution for focused scope\\n- Excellent re-rendering control\\n- Minimal overhead compared to Redux for this specific use case\\n**Alternatives Considered**: Redux (overkill for this focused fix)\\n\\n### Scroll Management: Custom React Hook\\n**Why**: Provides reusable, focused scroll position management\\n**Implementation**: useScrollPosition hook with throttling\\n\\n### Performance Optimization: React.memo + useMemo\\n**Why**: Prevents unnecessary re-renders during data updates\\n**Implementation**: Selective memoization of timeline components\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. ViewStateManager (Custom Hook)\\n**Responsibility**: Preserve and restore scroll position and view state\\n```\\nuseViewState() -> {\\n  scrollPosition: number,\\n  preservePosition: () => void,\\n  restorePosition: () => void\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 2. DataRefreshController (Custom Hook)\\n**Responsibility**: Manage data refresh without triggering view changes\\n```\\nuseDataRefresh() -> {\\n  refreshData: () => void,\\n  isRefreshing: boolean,\\n  lastUpdate: timestamp\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 3. TimelineContainer (Component)\\n**Responsibility**: Coordinate between data and view state\\n**Key Features**:\\n- Wraps existing timeline component\\n- Implements view state preservation\\n- Controls re-rendering scope\\n\\n### 4. MemoizedTimelineItems (Component)\\n**Responsibility**: Render timeline items with selective updates\\n**Key Features**:\\n- React.memo wrapper for performance\\n- Stable key generation for items\\n- Conditional re-rendering based on data changes\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n```\\nUser Interaction -> ViewState Preserved\\n                     \\u2193\\nData Refresh Triggered -> DataRefreshController\\n                     \\u2193\\nNew Data Received -> Selective Component Updates\\n                     \\u2193\\nView State Restored -> User Experience Maintained\\n```\\n\\n## File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nsrc/\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 timeline/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TimelineContainer.jsx          # Main container component\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 MemoizedTimelineItems.jsx      # Optimized timeline items\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502           \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 TimelineContainer.test.js\\n\\u2502           \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 integration.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useViewState.js                    # Scroll position management\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useDataRefresh.js                  # Data refresh control\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 __tests__/\\n\\u2502       \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 useViewState.test.js\\n\\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useDataRefresh.test.js\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 scrollUtils.js                     # Scroll position utilities\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 constants/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 refreshConstants.js                # Configuration constants\\n```\\n\\n## Data Model\\n\\n### ViewState Interface\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  scrollTop: number,\\n  scrollLeft: number,\\n  focusedItemId: string | null,\\n  timestamp: number\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### RefreshState Interface\\n```javascript\\n{\\n  isRefreshing: boolean,\\n  lastRefresh: Date,\\n  refreshCount: number,\\n  preserveView: boolean\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## API Integration\\n\\n### Existing Timeline API (Preserved)\\n- No changes to existing data fetch endpoints\\n- Maintains current real-time update mechanisms\\n- Preserves existing authentication and error handling\\n\\n### New Internal APIs\\n```javascript\\n// ViewState Management\\nviewStateManager.preserve()\\nviewStateManager.restore()\\nviewStateManager.getSnapshot()\\n\\n// Data Refresh Control\\ndataRefreshController.refreshWithViewPreservation()\\ndataRefreshController.setRefreshMode(mode)\\n```\\n\\n## Implementation Strategy\\n\\n### Phase 1: Core Infrastructure (2-3 days)\\n1. Create custom hooks (useViewState, useDataRefresh)\\n2. Implement scroll position utilities\\n3. Add basic test coverage\\n\\n### Phase 2: Component Integration (2-3 days)\\n1. Create TimelineContainer wrapper\\n2. Implement MemoizedTimelineItems\\n3. Integrate with existing timeline component\\n\\n### Phase 3: Testing & Refinement (2-3 days)\\n1. Comprehensive testing across browsers\\n2. Performance optimization\\n3. Edge case handling\\n\\n### Deployment Strategy\\n**Incremental Rollout**:\\n1. Feature flag implementation for A/B testing\\n2. Gradual rollout to user segments\\n3. Performance monitoring and rollback capability\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Unit Testing\\n- **Hooks Testing**: Custom hooks isolated testing with React Testing Library\\n- **Component Testing**: TimelineContainer and MemoizedTimelineItems\\n- **Utility Testing**: Scroll position calculation and preservation\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- **End-to-End Scenarios**: Full data refresh cycle with view preservation\\n- **Performance Testing**: Memory usage and re-render frequency\\n- **Cross-Browser Testing**: Scroll behavior consistency\\n\\n### Test Implementation\\n```javascript\\n// Example test structure\\ndescribe(\'ViewState Preservation\', () => {\\n  test(\'maintains scroll position during data refresh\', () => {\\n    // Test scroll position before/after refresh\\n  });\\n  \\n  test(\'prevents unexpected view jumps\', () => {\\n    // Test for view stability\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n\\n### Optimization Strategies\\n1. **Throttled Scroll Tracking**: Limit scroll position updates to 16ms intervals\\n2. **Selective Memoization**: Only memoize components that benefit from it\\n3. **Debounced Refresh**: Prevent rapid successive refresh calls\\n\\n### Memory Management\\n- Cleanup scroll listeners on component unmount\\n- Limit view state history to prevent memory leaks\\n- Use WeakMap for component-specific state storage\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### 1. Complete Timeline Component Rewrite\\n**Pros**: Clean slate approach, optimal performance\\n**Cons**: High risk, significant development time, potential for new bugs\\n**Decision**: Rejected due to scope constraints and risk\\n\\n### 2. Third-Party Scroll Management Library\\n**Pros**: Proven solution, extensive features\\n**Cons**: Additional dependency, potential overkill, bundle size increase\\n**Decision**: Rejected in favor of lightweight custom solution\\n\\n### 3. CSS-Only Solution\\n**Pros**: No JavaScript overhead, simple implementation\\n**Cons**: Limited control, browser compatibility issues\\n**Decision**: Rejected due to insufficient control over dynamic content\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk 1: Performance Degradation\\n**Mitigation**: Comprehensive performance testing, selective optimization\\n**Monitoring**: React DevTools profiling, lighthouse audits\\n\\n### Risk 2: Browser Compatibility\\n**Mitigation**: Cross-browser testing, progressive enhancement\\n**Fallback**: Graceful degradation to current behavior\\n\\n### Risk 3: Complex Edge Cases\\n**Mitigation**: Incremental rollout, extensive testing\\n**Strategy**: Feature flags for quick rollback if issues arise\\n\\n### Risk 4: Integration Conflicts\\n**Mitigation**: Minimal changes to existing components, wrapper-based approach\\n**Testing**: Isolated testing environment, staging deployment\\n\\n## Open Questions for User Review\\n\\n1. **Performance vs. Smoothness Trade-off**: Should we prioritize absolute minimal performance impact or smoothest user experience?\\n\\n2. **Fallback Strategy**: In case of scroll position restoration failure, should we maintain current position or reset to top?\\n\\n3. **Feature Flag Duration**: How long should the A/B testing period be before full rollout?\\n\\n4. **Refresh Frequency Impact**: Should this solution influence the current data refresh frequency, or maintain it exactly as-is?\\n\\n## Success Metrics & Monitoring\\n\\n### Primary Metrics\\n- **View Stability**: Zero unexpected scroll jumps during refresh (target: 100%)\\n- **User Experience**: Reduced user complaints about focus disruption\\n- **Performance**: No increase in render time (target: <5ms overhead)\\n\\n### Monitoring Implementation\\n- Custom analytics events for view preservation success/failure\\n- Performance monitoring integration\\n- User feedback collection mechanism\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a surgical solution to the focus disruption problem while maintaining compatibility with existing systems. The separation of concerns approach ensures maintainability, and the incremental implementation strategy minimizes risk while delivering measurable user experience improvements."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_0188ayUR8GHYNJZhUMzE7FfE', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_0188ayUR8GHYNJZhUMzE7FfE', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Frontend Tasks: Timeline Scroll Preservation\\n\\n## Task 1: Create Scroll Position Management Hook\\n- **Description**: Implement `useViewState` custom hook for scroll position tracking\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Hook provides methods to preserve and restore scroll position\\n  * Supports both vertical and horizontal scroll tracking\\n  * Minimal performance overhead\\n- **Dependencies**: None\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours\\n\\n## Task 2: Implement Data Refresh Controller Hook\\n- **Description**: Create `useDataRefresh` hook to manage data refresh without view disruption\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Controls data refresh lifecycle\\n  * Prevents unnecessary re-renders\\n  * Provides refresh status and last update timestamp\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1 (Scroll Position Hook)\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 3-5 hours\\n\\n## Task 3: Create Memoized Timeline Items Component\\n- **Description**: Develop optimized timeline items component with selective rendering\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Uses React.memo for performance\\n  * Generates stable keys for items\\n  * Conditionally updates only when data changes\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Task 4: Update Timeline Container\\n- **Description**: Modify existing HorizontalTimelineView to integrate new scroll preservation logic\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Preserves user\'s scroll position during data refresh\\n  * No unexpected view shifts\\n  * Maintains existing functionality\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2, Task 3\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 5-7 hours\\n\\n## Task 5: Implement Performance Monitoring\\n- **Description**: Add analytics and performance tracking for scroll preservation\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Tracks view stability events\\n  * Monitors render time overhead\\n  * Collects anonymous usage data for improvement\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 4\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours\\n\\n## Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n- **Description**: Comprehensive testing across different browsers and devices\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Verified on Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\\n  * Consistent behavior on desktop and mobile\\n  * No performance regressions\\n- **Dependencies**: All previous tasks\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Total Estimated Effort\\n- **Development Time**: 16-32 hours\\n- **Calendar Time**: 1-2 weeks\\n- **Complexity**: High precision refactoring\\n\\n## Recommended Implementation Order\\n1. Task 1: Scroll Position Hook\\n2. Task 2: Data Refresh Controller\\n3. Task 3: Memoized Timeline Items\\n4. Task 4: Timeline Container Update\\n5. Task 5: Performance Monitoring\\n6. Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n\\n## Open Questions for Clarification\\n1. What is the acceptable performance overhead for scroll preservation?\\n2. Are there any specific browsers or devices of particular concern?\\n3. Should we implement a fallback mechanism for scroll restoration failures?"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_012xzJ7YwPmLxuBfyHo8Sdry', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/tdd_coordinator', 'input_data': {'problem_description': "Fix timeline page data refresh focus disruption by implementing scroll position preservation during real-time data updates. The current implementation causes view jumps/resets when data refreshes. Need to implement custom hooks (useViewState, useDataRefresh) and update timeline component to maintain user's current view position while data updates occur in background.", 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend', 'test_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/__tests__', 'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_012xzJ7YwPmLxuBfyHo8Sdry', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write