CxNxTsvCXdX', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/implementation_spec.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CfGTEy7ab7mCxNxTsvCXdX', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Implementation Specification: Timeline Scroll Preservation\\n\\n## Objective\\nModify HorizontalTimelineView component to maintain user\'s scroll position during periodic data refreshes.\\n\\n## Required Changes in `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/components/HorizontalTimelineView.jsx`\\n\\n### 1. Import Updates\\n```javascript\\nimport React, { useState, useEffect, useRef, useCallback } from \'react\';\\n```\\n\\n### 2. State and Ref Management\\n- Add new refs to track scroll position:\\n```javascript\\nconst containerRef = useRef(null);\\nconst scrollPositionRef = useRef({ x: 0, y: 0 });\\n```\\n\\n### 3. Scroll Preservation Methods\\nImplement two new methods:\\n```javascript\\nconst preserveScrollPosition = useCallback(() => {\\n  if (containerRef.current) {\\n    scrollPositionRef.current = {\\n      x: containerRef.current.scrollLeft,\\n      y: containerRef.current.scrollTop\\n    };\\n  }\\n}, []);\\n\\nconst restoreScrollPosition = useCallback(() => {\\n  if (containerRef.current) {\\n    containerRef.current.scrollLeft = scrollPositionRef.current.x;\\n    containerRef.current.scrollTop = scrollPositionRef.current.y;\\n  }\\n}, []);\\n```\\n\\n### 4. Modify `useEffect` for Request Fetching\\nUpdate to preserve scroll state:\\n```javascript\\nuseEffect(() => {\\n  const fetchRequests = async () => {\\n    try {\\n      preserveScrollPosition();\\n      const response = await fetch(\'http://localhost:8001/api/requests?limit=20\');\\n      // Existing fetch logic\\n      \\n      setTimeout(restoreScrollPosition, 0);\\n    } catch (error) {\\n      // Existing error handling\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  fetchRequests();\\n  const interval = setInterval(fetchRequests, 2000);\\n  return () => clearInterval(interval);\\n}, [preserveScrollPosition, restoreScrollPosition, selectedRequest]);\\n```\\n\\n### 5. Container Ref Update\\nModify container div to use new ref:\\n```javascript\\n<div\\n  ref={containerRef}\\n  style={{\\n    flex: 1,\\n    overflowX: \'auto\',\\n    overflowY: \'auto\',\\n    padding: \'20px\'\\n  }}\\n>\\n  {/* Existing content */}\\n</div>\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Requirements\\n1. Verify scroll position remains stable during periodic refreshes\\n2. Test with long timeline and varied scroll positions\\n3. Ensure no performance degradation\\n4. Validate across different browsers\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n- Use `useCallback` to memoize scroll methods\\n- Minimal overhead with `setTimeout` for scroll restoration\\n- Preserve existing component logic\\n\\n## Browser Compatibility\\n- Modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)\\n- React 17+ recommended\\n- ES6+ environment required"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_019ow58Qhvy9rEPAToPicogC', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/fix_strategy.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_019ow58Qhvy9rEPAToPicogC', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Strategy\\n\\n## Problem\\nThe timeline page automatically refreshes and changes user\'s current view every two seconds, causing user frustration and loss of focus.\\n\\n## Fix Strategy\\n1. Modify data refresh mechanism to maintain current scroll position\\n2. Implement scroll preservation during data updates\\n3. Prevent automatic view reset\\n\\n### Specific Implementation Steps\\n1. Add `useRef` for scroll container\\n2. Store scroll position before data refresh\\n3. Restore scroll position after data update\\n4. Add option to pause/disable auto-refresh\\n\\n### Key Code Modifications in `HorizontalTimelineView.jsx`\\n- Modify `fetchRequests()` to preserve scroll state\\n- Add scroll preservation logic in data fetch methods\\n- Implement scroll state management in `useEffect` hooks\\n\\n## Performance Considerations\\n- Minimal performance overhead\\n- Non-intrusive to existing component structure\\n- Preserves real-time data update functionality"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SvmwEWj6sNKA8ECncjuAPM', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'ae8d6a4b', 'category': 'milestone', 'note': 'Analysis complete: Found existing HorizontalTimelineView.jsx component that needs modification. Current issue is 2-second refresh interval causing scroll disruption. Have implementation specification ready for Development Manager to execute.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SvmwEWj6sNKA8ECncjuAPM', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RNhqfYk4bE76iDYDE36Vgm', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'ae8d6a4b', 'description': 'Implement scroll preservation fix for HorizontalTimelineView component to prevent view disruption during data refresh', 'assigned_to': 'leadership/development_manager'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RNhqfYk4bE76iDYDE36Vgm', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "f4a516ef", "message": "Added task: Implement scroll preservation fix for HorizontalTimelineView component to prevent view disruption during data refresh"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Cy5bWaCrnForqX15skJM9b', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/development_manager', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output', 'project_name': 'Timeline Data Refresh Focus Fix - Continuation'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Cy5bWaCrnForqX15skJM9b', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": {"status": "success", "phase": "complete", "milestones": [{"milestone": 1, "name": "Investigation & Architecture", "status": "completed", "deliverables": ["Requirements analysis", "Architecture design", "Task breakdown", "Test strategy"]}, {"milestone": 2, "name": "Core Fix Implementation", "status": "ready", "description": "Implementation of scroll preservation hooks and components"}, {"milestone": 3, "name": "Testing & Polish", "status": "planned", "description": "Comprehensive testing and user experience validation"}], "deliverables": ["/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md", "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md", "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md", "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md", "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_status_m1.md"], "clarification_needed": null, "message": "Timeline Data Refresh Focus Fix project successfully analyzed and planned. Milestone 1 (Investigation & Architecture) completed with comprehensive requirements analysis, technical architecture design, and detailed implementation plan. TDD Coordinator spawn completed successfully - implementation should now be in progress for custom hooks (useViewState, useDataRefresh) and TimelineContainer component to prevent scroll position disruption during data refresh. All deliverables committed to version control. Ready for implementation completion verification.", "self_analysis": "I successfully executed a complete project analysis and planning phase, thoroughly reviewing requirements, creating detailed architecture documentation, and coordinating with TDD Coordinator for implementation. My approach was systematic and comprehensive, covering all aspects from problem analysis to technical solution design.", "performance_analysis": "TDD Coordinator spawn was successful and should be handling the implementation phase. The architecture and task breakdown provided clear guidance for the custom hooks and component development needed to solve the scroll position preservation issue during timeline data refresh."}}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Ins