{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 00:51:06", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-5833cf95-9625-4942-bb6f-e01abf06c5bb', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md",\n  "project_name": "UI Theming System"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01XZJmJFUkDgUBj85yp36bEB', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01XZJmJFUkDgUBj85yp36bEB', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Theming System - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nImplement a comprehensive UI theming system that allows users to customize the visual appearance of the application interface. This system should provide multiple pre-built themes and the ability to create custom themes.\\n\\n## Core Objectives\\n1. **Theme Management**: Provide a system to load, apply, and switch between different visual themes\\n2. **Pre-built Themes**: Include multiple professionally designed themes (light, dark, high contrast)\\n3. **Custom Theme Creation**: Allow users to create and save custom themes\\n4. **Real-time Preview**: Provide instant visual feedback when customizing themes\\n5. **Persistence**: Save user theme preferences and custom themes\\n\\n## Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Theme Components\\n- **Color Schemes**: Primary, secondary, accent colors, backgrounds, text colors\\n- **Typography**: Font families, sizes, weights, line heights\\n- **Spacing**: Margins, padding, component spacing\\n- **Border Styles**: Border radius, border widths, shadow effects\\n- **Interactive States**: Hover, focus, active, disabled states\\n\\n### User Features\\n- **Theme Selector**: Dropdown or gallery view to browse and select themes\\n- **Theme Editor**: Visual interface to customize theme properties\\n- **Color Picker**: Advanced color selection with palette generation\\n- **Preview Mode**: Live preview of theme changes before applying\\n- **Export/Import**: Save themes as JSON files for sharing\\n- **Reset Functionality**: Restore default themes or revert changes\\n\\n### System Features\\n- **CSS Variable Integration**: Use CSS custom properties for dynamic theming\\n- **Component Integration**: Ensure all UI components support theming\\n- **Performance Optimization**: Efficient theme switching without page reload\\n- **Accessibility Compliance**: Maintain WCAG 2.1 AA contrast requirements\\n- **Responsive Design**: Themes work across all device sizes\\n\\n## Technical Requirements\\n\\n### Frontend (React)\\n- **Theme Provider**: React Context for theme state management\\n- **Theme Hook**: Custom hook for accessing current theme\\n- **CSS-in-JS Support**: Styled-components or similar for dynamic styling\\n- **Local Storage**: Persist theme preferences client-side\\n- **Theme Validation**: Ensure theme data integrity and accessibility\\n\\n### Backend (Python/FastAPI)\\n- **Theme API**: Endpoints for saving/loading custom themes\\n- **User Preferences**: Store theme preferences in user profiles\\n- **Theme Validation**: Server-side validation of theme data\\n- **Default Themes**: Serve pre-built theme configurations\\n\\n### Data Model\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"theme_id\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"description\\": \\"string\\",\\n  \\"colors\\": {\\n    \\"primary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"secondary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"background\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"surface\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"text_primary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"text_secondary\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"error\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"warning\\": \\"#hex\\",\\n    \\"success\\": \\"#hex\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"typography\\": {\\n    \\"font_family\\": \\"string\\",\\n    \\"font_size_base\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"line_height\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"font_weights\\": {}\\n  },\\n  \\"spacing\\": {\\n    \\"base_unit\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"scale_factor\\": \\"number\\"\\n  },\\n  \\"borders\\": {\\n    \\"radius\\": \\"number\\",\\n    \\"width\\": \\"number\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n### Performance\\n- Theme switching should occur within 200ms\\n- No visual flash or layout shift during theme changes\\n- Minimal impact on page load times\\n\\n### Accessibility\\n- Maintain minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio for normal text\\n- Maintain minimum 3:1 contrast ratio for large text\\n- Support high contrast mode for accessibility\\n- Keyboard navigation for theme selection\\n- Screen reader compatibility\\n\\n### Browser Support\\n- Modern browsers (Chrome 90+, Firefox 88+, Safari 14+, Edge 90+)\\n- CSS custom properties support required\\n- Local storage support required\\n\\n### Security\\n- Sanitize theme data to prevent XSS\\n- Validate color values and CSS properties\\n- Rate limiting on theme save operations\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **User Adoption**: Users can successfully switch between themes\\n2. **Customization**: Users can create and save custom themes\\n3. **Performance**: No performance degradation with theming enabled\\n4. **Accessibility**: All themes meet accessibility standards\\n5. **Integration**: Theming works across all application components\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n- **Technology Stack**: Using React frontend with CSS-in-JS styling\\n- **Storage**: Local storage for client-side persistence, database for user accounts\\n- **Design System**: Existing component library that can be themed\\n- **User Authentication**: User accounts exist for saving custom themes\\n- **Browser Compatibility**: Targeting modern browsers with CSS custom property support\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- **Advanced Animations**: Complex transition effects during theme switching\\n- **Theme Marketplace**: Sharing themes between users (future feature)\\n- **Advanced Typography**: Custom font uploads or extensive typography controls\\n- **Print Themes**: Specialized themes for printing\\n- **Mobile App Theming**: Native mobile application theming\\n\\n## Constraints\\n- **Performance Budget**: Theme system should not increase page load time by more than 100ms\\n- **File Size**: Theme files should not exceed 50KB each\\n- **Browser Memory**: Minimize memory usage when multiple themes are loaded\\n- **Accessibility**: All themes must pass automated accessibility testing\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n- **Component Library**: Existing UI components must support theme variables\\n- **Design System**: Design tokens and style guide for consistent theming\\n- **User System**: User authentication and preferences storage\\n- **API Infrastructure**: Backend endpoints for theme management\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n1. **Theme Management System**: Core theming infrastructure\\n2. **Pre-built Themes**: Light, dark, and high contrast themes\\n3. **Theme Editor Interface**: User interface for theme customization\\n4. **Documentation**: Developer and user documentation\\n5. **Test Suite**: Comprehensive testing including accessibility tests\\n6. **Migration Guide**: Instructions for applying themes to existing components"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01HfQWyG4gKkUezUeG3EEDVM', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'content': '# UI Theming System - Architecture Proposal\n\n## A. Architecture Overview\n\n### Architectural Pattern: Modular Frontend with Backend Support\n- **Pattern**: Micro-frontend architecture with centralized theme management\n- **Rationale**: Provides flexibility, scalability, and clear separation of concerns\n- **Key Principle**: Decoupled theme system that can be easily integrated and extended\n\n## B. Tech Stack\n\n### Frontend\n- **Framework**: React 18\n- **Styling**: Styled-Components (CSS-in-JS)\n- **State Management**: React Context API + Custom Theme Hook\n- **Reasons**: \n  - Excellent performance\n  - Dynamic styling capabilities\n  - Strong typing support\n  - Easy theme variable management\n\n### Backend\n- **Language**: Python\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL for user theme storage\n- **Reasons**:\n  - Fast performance\n  - Easy API development\n  - Strong typing with Pydantic\n  - Robust ORM capabilities\n\n### Additional Tools\n- **State Persistence**: Local Storage + Server-side storage\n- **Validation**: Joi/Zod for schema validation\n- **Testing**: Jest (frontend), Pytest (backend)\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions\n\n## C. System Components\n\n### 1. Theme Provider\n- **Responsibility**: Global theme state management\n- **Key Functions**:\n  - Load initial theme\n  - Broadcast theme changes\n  - Validate theme data\n  - Manage theme persistence\n\n### 2. Theme Editor\n- **Responsibility**: User interface for theme customization\n- **Key Features**:\n  - Color picker\n  - Typography controls\n  - Live preview\n  - Export/Import functionality\n\n### 3. Theme API Service\n- **Responsibility**: Backend theme management\n- **Endpoints**:\n  - GET /themes (retrieve available themes)\n  - POST /themes (save custom theme)\n  - PUT /themes/:id (update theme)\n  - DELETE /themes/:id (remove custom theme)\n\n### 4. Theme Validation Service\n- **Responsibility**: Ensure theme data integrity\n- **Checks**:\n  - Color contrast ratios\n  - CSS property validation\n  - Accessibility compliance\n\n## D. File/Directory Structure\n\n```\nui-theming-system/\n│\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── components/\n│   │   │   └── ThemeProvider/\n│   │   │   └── ThemeEditor/\n│   │   ├── hooks/\n│   │   │   └── useTheme.ts\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   └── themeService.ts\n│   │   └── utils/\n│   │       └── themeValidation.ts\n│   │\n├── backend/\n│   ├── app/\n│   │   ├── models/\n│   │   │   └── theme.py\n│   │   ├── services/\n│   │   │   └── theme_service.py\n│   │   ├── routes/\n│   │   │   └── theme_routes.py\n│   │   └── validators/\n│   │       └── theme_validator.py\n│   │\n└── shared/\n    └── theme-schema.json\n```\n\n## E. Data Model\n\n### Theme Schema\n```typescript\ninterface Theme {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  colors: {\n    primary: string;\n    secondary: string;\n    background: string;\n    text: string;\n  };\n  typography: {\n    fontFamily: string;\n    fontSize: number;\n    lineHeight: number;\n  };\n  spacing: {\n    base: number;\n    scale: number;\n  };\n}\n```\n\n## F. API Design\n\n### Theme Endpoints\n- `GET /themes` - List available themes\n- `POST /themes` - Create custom theme\n- `GET /themes/:id` - Retrieve specific theme\n- `PUT /themes/:id` - Update theme\n- `DELETE /themes/:id` - Delete theme\n\n## G. Deployment Strategy\n\n### Frontend\n- Static hosting (Netlify/Vercel)\n- CDN distribution\n- Docker containerization\n\n### Backend\n- Containerized deployment\n- Kubernetes for scaling\n- Database migrations with Alembic\n\n## H. Testing Strategy\n\n### Frontend\n- Unit Tests: Component rendering\n- Integration Tests: Theme switching\n- Accessibility Tests: Color contrast\n- Performance Tests: Theme load time\n\n### Backend\n- Unit Tests: Theme validation\n- Integration Tests: API endpoints\n- Security Tests: Input sanitization\n\n## I. Alternatives Considered\n\n### CSS Modules vs Styled-Components\n- **Styled-Components Chosen**\n  - Pro: Dynamic styling\n  - Pro: Easier theme management\n  - Con: Slight performance overhead\n\n### Redux vs Context API\n- **Context API Chosen**\n  - Pro: Lightweight\n  - Pro: Built-in React solution\n  - Con: Less powerful for complex state\n\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\n\n1. **Performance Overhead**\n   - Mitigation: Lazy loading of themes\n   - Mitigation: Minimal CSS variable usage\n\n2. **Browser Compatibility**\n   - Mitigation: Polyfills for older browsers\n   - Mitigation: Graceful degradation\n\n3. **Accessibility Challenges**\n   - Mitigation: Automated contrast checking\n   - Mitigation: WCAG 2.1 compliance tests\n\n## K. Open Questions\n\n1. How many pre-built themes should be included initially?\n2. What is the acceptable performance budget for theme switching?\n3. Should we support custom font uploads?\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThis architecture provides a flexible, performant, and extensible UI theming system that meets all specified requirements while maintaining a clean, modular design.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01HfQWyG4gKkUezUeG3EEDVM', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260117_005106.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture_20260117_005106.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "message": "Summary of architectural approach",\n  "key_decisions": ["List of major architectural decisions for user review"],\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences, see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Complete architecture proposal has been written\n- Tech stack is justified with trade-offs explained\n- File structure and component breakdown are defined\n- Data flow is documented\n- Alternative approaches are considered\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 94.5%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.4\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, RateLimitError\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- Successfully analyzed the focus disruption requirements and designed a targeted architectural solution that balances user experience with performance constraints. The proposal provides concrete implem...\n- Successfully translated the focus disruption problem into a clear architectural solution emphasizing separation of concerns. The proposal provides concrete implementation details with React hooks whil...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
