rwxr-xr-x@   7 mattbillock  staff    224 Jan 14 23:40 whimsical-agent-names\\n", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01UCL7PgJEWVZq9sBd27uA9s', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# UI Theming System - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nThis project implements a comprehensive UI theming system with multiple pre-built themes and custom theme creation capabilities.\n\n## Milestone 1: Core Theming Infrastructure (Week 1-2)\n**Objective**: Establish the foundation for the theming system with basic theme switching capabilities.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- CSS custom properties architecture\n- React theme context and provider\n- Basic theme hook implementation\n- Theme data model and validation\n- Local storage persistence\n- Basic theme loading/switching functionality\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Theme context can be consumed by any component\n- CSS custom properties update dynamically when theme changes\n- Theme preferences persist across browser sessions\n- Theme data validation prevents invalid configurations\n- No visual flash during theme switching\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n## Milestone 2: Pre-built Themes and Theme Selector (Week 3)\n**Objective**: Implement pre-built themes and user interface for theme selection.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Light, dark, and high contrast themes\n- Theme selector component (dropdown/gallery)\n- Theme preview functionality\n- Component integration with theming system\n- Accessibility compliance validation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- All three pre-built themes are fully functional\n- Theme selector provides clear visual preview\n- All UI components properly respond to theme changes\n- WCAG 2.1 AA contrast requirements are met\n- Keyboard navigation works for theme selection\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (core infrastructure)\n\n## Milestone 3: Custom Theme Creation and Editor (Week 4-5)\n**Objective**: Enable users to create, edit, and manage custom themes.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Theme editor interface\n- Color picker component\n- Typography and spacing controls\n- Real-time theme preview\n- Custom theme save/load functionality\n- Theme export/import (JSON)\n- Theme reset functionality\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Users can customize all theme properties\n- Real-time preview shows changes immediately\n- Custom themes can be saved and reloaded\n- Theme export/import works with valid JSON\n- Reset functionality restores original themes\n- Theme editor is accessible and intuitive\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (theme selector and base themes)\n\n## Milestone 4: Backend Integration and User Preferences (Week 6)\n**Objective**: Integrate with backend for theme persistence and user preference management.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Theme API endpoints (save, load, delete themes)\n- User preference storage integration\n- Theme synchronization across devices\n- Server-side theme validation\n- Rate limiting and security measures\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Custom themes persist across devices for logged-in users\n- API endpoints handle theme CRUD operations\n- Server validates theme data for security\n- Rate limiting prevents abuse\n- Theme sync works reliably\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 3 (custom theme creation), User authentication system\n\n## Milestone 5: Performance Optimization and Testing (Week 7)\n**Objective**: Optimize performance and ensure comprehensive test coverage.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- Performance optimizations for theme switching\n- Comprehensive test suite (unit, integration, accessibility)\n- Browser compatibility testing\n- Performance benchmarking\n- Documentation and user guides\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Theme switching occurs within 200ms\n- All tests pass including accessibility tests\n- Compatible with target browsers\n- Documentation is complete and accurate\n- No memory leaks or performance regressions\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 4 (complete system)\n\n## Success Metrics\n- **Performance**: Theme switching < 200ms, no layout shift\n- **Accessibility**: All themes pass WCAG 2.1 AA standards\n- **User Experience**: Intuitive theme selection and creation\n- **Compatibility**: Works across all target browsers\n- **Test Coverage**: >90% code coverage with passing accessibility tests\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n- **CSS Custom Property Support**: Graceful degradation for older browsers\n- **Performance Impact**: Regular performance monitoring during development\n- **Accessibility Compliance**: Automated and manual accessibility testing\n- **User Experience**: User testing and feedback integration\n\n## Resource Requirements\n- **Frontend Developer**: React, CSS-in-JS, accessibility expertise\n- **Backend Developer**: Python/FastAPI, API design\n- **UI/UX Designer**: Theme design, accessibility consultation\n- **QA Engineer**: Testing, accessibility validation'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01UCL7PgJEWVZq9sBd27uA9s', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260117_005035.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260117_005035.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01RUcQz7egbDpbrvnCwibvUG', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'leadership/system_architect', 'input_data': {'requirements_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md', 'output_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md', 'project_name': 'UI Theming System'}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01RUcQz7egbDpbrvnCwibvUG', 'content': '{"success": true, "result": null}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Mh3x41AjSxG3UqYad8Hd43', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Mh3x41AjSxG3UqYad8Hd43', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# UI Theming System - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## A. Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern: Modular Frontend with Backend Support\\n- **Pattern**: Micro-frontend architecture with centralized theme management\\n- **Rationale**: Provides flexibility, scalability, and clear separation of concerns\\n- **Key Principle**: Decoupled theme system that can be easily integrated and extended\\n\\n## B. Tech Stack\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- **Framework**: React 18\\n- **Styling**: Styled-Components (CSS-in-JS)\\n- **State Management**: React Context API + Custom Theme Hook\\n- **Reasons**: \\n  - Excellent performance\\n  - Dynamic styling capabilities\\n  - Strong typing support\\n  - Easy theme variable management\\n\\n### Backend\\n- **Language**: Python\\n- **Framework**: FastAPI\\n- **Database**: PostgreSQL for user theme storage\\n- **Reasons**:\\n  - Fast performance\\n  - Easy API development\\n  - Strong typing with Pydantic\\n  - Robust ORM capabilities\\n\\n### Additional Tools\\n- **State Persistence**: Local Storage + Server-side storage\\n- **Validation**: Joi/Zod for schema validation\\n- **Testing**: Jest (frontend), Pytest (backend)\\n- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions\\n\\n## C. System Components\\n\\n### 1. Theme Provider\\n- **Responsibility**: Global theme state management\\n- **Key Functions**:\\n  - Load initial theme\\n  - Broadcast theme changes\\n  - Validate theme data\\n  - Manage theme persistence\\n\\n### 2. Theme Editor\\n- **Responsibility**: User interface for theme customization\\n- **Key Features**:\\n  - Color picker\\n  - Typography controls\\n  - Live preview\\n  - Export/Import functionality\\n\\n### 3. Theme API Service\\n- **Responsibility**: Backend theme management\\n- **Endpoints**:\\n  - GET /themes (retrieve available themes)\\n  - POST /themes (save custom theme)\\n  - PUT /themes/:id (update theme)\\n  - DELETE /themes/:id (remove custom theme)\\n\\n### 4. Theme Validation Service\\n- **Responsibility**: Ensure theme data integrity\\n- **Checks**:\\n  - Color contrast ratios\\n  - CSS property validation\\n  - Accessibility compliance\\n\\n## D. File/Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\nui-theming-system/\\n\\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 frontend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 src/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 components/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeProvider/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 ThemeEditor/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 hooks/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 useTheme.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeService.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 utils/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 themeValidation.ts\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 backend/\\n\\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 app/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 models/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 services/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme_service.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u251c\\u2500\\u2500 routes/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme_routes.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502   \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 validators/\\n\\u2502   \\u2502       \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme_validator.py\\n\\u2502   \\u2502\\n\\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 shared/\\n    \\u2514\\u2500\\u2500 theme-schema.json\\n```\\n\\n## E. Data Model\\n\\n### Theme Schema\\n```typescript\\ninterface Theme {\\n  id: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  colors: {\\n    primary: string;\\n    secondary: string;\\n    background: string;\\n    text: string;\\n  };\\n  typography: {\\n    fontFamily: string;\\n    fontSize: number;\\n    lineHeight: number;\\n  };\\n  spacing: {\\n    base: number;\\n    scale: number;\\n  };\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## F. API Design\\n\\n### Theme Endpoints\\n- `GET /themes` - List available themes\\n- `POST /themes` - Create custom theme\\n- `GET /themes/:id` - Retrieve specific theme\\n- `PUT /themes/:id` - Update theme\\n- `DELETE /themes/:id` - Delete theme\\n\\n## G. Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Static hosting (Netlify/Vercel)\\n- CDN distribution\\n- Docker containerization\\n\\n### Backend\\n- Containerized deployment\\n- Kubernetes for scaling\\n- Database migrations with Alembic\\n\\n## H. Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Frontend\\n- Unit Tests: Component rendering\\n- Integration Tests: Theme switching\\n- Accessibility Tests: Color contrast\\n- Performance Tests: Theme load time\\n\\n### Backend\\n- Unit Tests: Theme validation\\n- Integration Tests: API endpoints\\n- Security Tests: Input sanitization\\n\\n## I. Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### CSS Modules vs Styled-Components\\n- **Styled-Components Chosen**\\n  - Pro: Dynamic styling\\n  - Pro: Easier theme management\\n  - Con: Slight performance overhead\\n\\n### Redux vs Context API\\n- **Context API Chosen**\\n  - Pro: Lightweight\\n  - Pro: Built-in React solution\\n  - Con: Less powerful for complex state\\n\\n## J. Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n1. **Performance Overhead**\\n   - Mitigation: Lazy loading of themes\\n   - Mitigation: Minimal CSS variable usage\\n\\n2. **Browser Compatibility**\\n   - Mitigation: Polyfills for older browsers\\n   - Mitigation: Graceful degradation\\n\\n3. **Accessibility Challenges**\\n   - Mitigation: Automated contrast checking\\n   - Mitigation: WCAG 2.1 compliance tests\\n\\n## K. Open Questions\\n\\n1. How many pre-built themes should be included initially?\\n2. What is the acceptable performance budget for theme switching?\\n3. Should we support custom font uploads?\\n\\n## Conclusion\\n\\nThis architecture provides a flexible, performant, and extensible UI theming system that meets all specified requirements while maintaining a clean, modular design."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Development Manager has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 61.9%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.1\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Focus on completing tasks successfully - your success rate needs improvement.\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively managed project completion by thoroughly reviewing the milestone status document, updating project tracking records, and creating comprehensive completion documentation. My approach focu...\n- Executed a comprehensive validation project with systematic approach, leveraging multiple agents to design, implement, and validate the A/B testing framework. Demonstrated ability to drive project fro...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
