nt', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VF7TfXFv2MvzfLg2k4pArN', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'ae8d6a4b', 'category': 'general', 'note': 'Found modifications in HorizontalTimelineView.jsx - some implementation appears to be in progress. File has been modified to accept initialRequestId prop and prevent auto-reselection. However, no scroll preservation logic visible yet. Need to verify complete implementation.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VF7TfXFv2MvzfLg2k4pArN', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01HdhNx5pjguTvip5Zq3hVtE', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/hooks -name "*viewState*" -o -name "*ViewState*" -o -name "*scroll*" -o -name "*Scroll*" 2>/dev/null || echo "no scroll/view state hooks found"'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01HdhNx5pjguTvip5Zq3hVtE', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01JT93unAZP2NEjC1CRj52kQ', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/tests -name "*horizontal*" -o -name "*timeline*" -o -name "*scroll*" 2>/dev/null || echo "no tests found"'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01JT93unAZP2NEjC1CRj52kQ', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": ""}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01EpNV3frFPK9xEaZQYURh6X', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01EpNV3frFPK9xEaZQYURh6X', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Frontend Tasks: Timeline Scroll Preservation\\n\\n## Task 1: Create Scroll Position Management Hook\\n- **Description**: Implement `useViewState` custom hook for scroll position tracking\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Hook provides methods to preserve and restore scroll position\\n  * Supports both vertical and horizontal scroll tracking\\n  * Minimal performance overhead\\n- **Dependencies**: None\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours\\n\\n## Task 2: Implement Data Refresh Controller Hook\\n- **Description**: Create `useDataRefresh` hook to manage data refresh without view disruption\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Controls data refresh lifecycle\\n  * Prevents unnecessary re-renders\\n  * Provides refresh status and last update timestamp\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1 (Scroll Position Hook)\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 3-5 hours\\n\\n## Task 3: Create Memoized Timeline Items Component\\n- **Description**: Develop optimized timeline items component with selective rendering\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Uses React.memo for performance\\n  * Generates stable keys for items\\n  * Conditionally updates only when data changes\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Task 4: Update Timeline Container\\n- **Description**: Modify existing HorizontalTimelineView to integrate new scroll preservation logic\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Preserves user\'s scroll position during data refresh\\n  * No unexpected view shifts\\n  * Maintains existing functionality\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2, Task 3\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 5-7 hours\\n\\n## Task 5: Implement Performance Monitoring\\n- **Description**: Add analytics and performance tracking for scroll preservation\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Tracks view stability events\\n  * Monitors render time overhead\\n  * Collects anonymous usage data for improvement\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 4\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours\\n\\n## Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n- **Description**: Comprehensive testing across different browsers and devices\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Verified on Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\\n  * Consistent behavior on desktop and mobile\\n  * No performance regressions\\n- **Dependencies**: All previous tasks\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Total Estimated Effort\\n- **Development Time**: 16-32 hours\\n- **Calendar Time**: 1-2 weeks\\n- **Complexity**: High precision refactoring\\n\\n## Recommended Implementation Order\\n1. Task 1: Scroll Position Hook\\n2. Task 2: Data Refresh Controller\\n3. Task 3: Memoized Timeline Items\\n4. Task 4: Timeline Container Update\\n5. Task 5: Performance Monitoring\\n6. Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n\\n## Open Questions for Clarification\\n1. What is the acceptable performance overhead for scroll preservation?\\n2. Are there any specific browsers or devices of particular concern?\\n3. Should we implement a fallback mechanism for scroll restoration failures?"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ShGbdPzKxcCZa9oin2Vsa9', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01ShGbdPzKxcCZa9oin2Vsa9', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Test Strategy: Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix\\n\\n## Objective\\nEnsure scroll preservation in HorizontalTimelineView during data refresh, preventing user focus disruption.\\n\\n## Test Coverage Strategy\\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 90% for custom hooks and utility functions\\n- **Integration Test Coverage**: 100% for view state management\\n- **End-to-End Test Coverage**: Critical user interaction flows\\n\\n## Test Task Breakdown\\n\\n### 1. useViewState Hook Tests\\n- [ ] Verify scroll position tracking\\n- [ ] Test position preservation mechanism\\n- [ ] Validate scroll restoration functionality\\n- [ ] Check memory management and cleanup\\n\\n### 2. useDataRefresh Hook Tests\\n- [ ] Validate data refresh without view disruption\\n- [ ] Test refresh state management\\n- [ ] Verify performance during rapid successive refreshes\\n- [ ] Ensure no unexpected re-renders\\n\\n### 3. TimelineContainer Component Tests\\n- [ ] Confirm view state isolation\\n- [ ] Test integration of view state and data refresh\\n- [ ] Validate memoization effectiveness\\n- [ ] Check cross-browser scroll behavior\\n\\n### 4. Performance and Edge Case Tests\\n- [ ] Measure render time overhead\\n- [ ] Test with large datasets\\n- [ ] Validate behavior under slow network conditions\\n- [ ] Check memory usage during extended use\\n\\n### 5. End-to-End Interaction Tests\\n- [ ] Simulate real-world user scrolling during data refresh\\n- [ ] Test multiple rapid data updates\\n- [ ] Verify no unexpected view shifts\\n- [ ] Validate smooth user experience\\n\\n## Testing Tools and Frameworks\\n- **Unit Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library\\n- **Performance Testing**: React DevTools Profiler\\n- **E2E Testing**: Playwright\\n- **Scroll Simulation**: Custom scroll event generators\\n\\n## Specific Test Scenarios\\n\\n### Positive Scenarios\\n1. User scrolls midway through timeline\\n2. Data refresh occurs without changing scroll position\\n3. Multiple rapid data updates\\n4. Large dataset with continuous updates\\n\\n### Negative/Edge Scenarios\\n1. Extremely fast scroll during refresh\\n2. Refresh during scroll momentum\\n3. Low-performance devices\\n4. Interrupted network conditions\\n\\n## Performance Benchmarks\\n- **Render Time**: &lt; 5ms overhead\\n- **Memory Usage**: No significant increase\\n- **Scroll Smoothness**: 60 FPS minimum\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation Tests\\n- Verify fallback mechanisms\\n- Test feature flag integration\\n- Validate graceful degradation\\n\\n## Recommended Test Sequence\\n1. Unit tests for individual hooks\\n2. Component integration tests\\n3. Performance benchmark tests\\n4. End-to-end user flow tests\\n5. Cross-browser compatibility tests\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign testing\\n- Testing unrelated components\\n- Network layer testing beyond current implementation\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Comprehensive test coverage report\\n- Performance metrics documentation\\n- Recommendations for further optimization"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01158rg78fd7hHZVoeMh4VyL', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'ae8d6a4b', 'category': 'issue', 'note': 'Implementation appears incomplete: Only basic prop handling added to HorizontalTimelineView.jsx. Missing core scroll preservation hooks (useViewState, useDataRefresh), TimelineContainer wrapper component, and comprehensive testing. Need to complete implementation according to architecture and task specifications.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01158rg78fd7hHZVoeMh4VyL', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SMFLuZFSjWiVTGao2AQwHt', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordination/frontend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'task_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src', 'milestone_number': 1}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SMFLuZFSjWiVTGao2AQwHt', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Unknown agent type: coordination/frontend_coordinator. Agent definition file not found."}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js, .jsx, tests)\n**Rule**: If it\'s code → delegate to leadership/program_coordinator\n\n### Your Authority:\nResource allocation decisions\nWhen to escalate to user\nApprove/reject Development Manager requests\nDecide when project complete\nFinal say on requirements met\n\n### Escalate to User (needs_user_input) When:\n**Multiple equally valid approaches** with significant trade-offs (e.g., real-time vs polling, SQL vs NoSQL)\n**User\'s intent is genuinely unclear** (e.g., "make it better" without context)\n**Business decisions** that affect cost, privacy, or legal compliance\n**Blockers requiring external action** (API keys, access, approvals)\n**Major architectural pivots** after initial implementation\n\n**DO NOT ask for**:\nStandard technology choices (use modern defaults)\nCommon UI patterns (use industry best practices)\nDeployment details (assume standard cloud)\nTesting approaches (use TDD)\nCode organization (use standard patterns)\n\n### Anti-Patterns (What NOT to Do)\n\n**Scope Constraints:**\nDo NOT implement features not explicitly in the user\'s vision\nNEVER expand project scope without user approval\nDo NOT add "nice to have" features beyond the core requirements\nNEVER bypass the Development Manager to coordinate directly with developers\n\n**Delegation Constraints:**\nDo NOT write code directly - ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager\nNEVER attempt to write files with code extensions (.py, .js, .jsx, etc.)\nDo NOT spawn more than 3 major agents in parallel without reviewing results\nNEVER skip phases (requirements → architecture → implementation)\n\n**Process Constraints:**\nDo NOT retry the same approach more than 3 times without changing strategy\nNEVER proceed without a valid project_id from project_tracking\nDo NOT skip requirement validation before spawning Development Manager\nNEVER consider project complete without verification from Development Manager\n\n**Communication Constraints:**\nDo NOT ask users for standard implementation details\nNEVER present technical jargon without explanation\nDo NOT provide vague status updates - be specific about what\'s done and what\'s left\nNEVER report success if any tests are failing\n\n**Safety Constraints:**\nDo NOT approve destructive operations without user confirmation\nNEVER ignore errors from spawned agents - escalate or handle explicitly\nDo NOT continue if Development Manager reports a blocking issue\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n\n**Performance Insight (Auto-Applied):**\nAgent Executive Director has a success rate below 75%. Consider reviewing recent failures and adjusting definition.\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "user_vision": "string - what user wants to build and why",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create project artifacts",\n  "context": "string - background, constraints (optional)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|failed|needs_user_input",\n  "project_id": "string - ID from project tracking system",\n  "project_name": "string",\n  "phase": "string - requirements|architecture|planning|implementation|complete",\n  "summary": "string - what has been accomplished",\n  "deliverables": "array of created file paths",\n  "user_question": "string - question for user if needs_user_input (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status message",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (see Self-Improvement Directive)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of spawned agents\' collective performance (see Self-Improvement Directive)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Project completed: implementation done, tests passing, docs complete\n- User approved final deliverable OR user terminated project\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 54.3%\n- Average iterations per task: 11.6\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Focus on completing tasks successfully - your success rate needs improvement.\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- I effectively managed the milestone completion by systematically tracking project progress, validating requirements, and ensuring all objectives were met with high-quality implementation and testing.\n- Successfully orchestrated complex model validation project by coordinating multiple agents, leveraging systematic approach to validate TDD Coordinator performance improvements. Project demonstrated ab...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided