component with selective rendering\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Uses React.memo for performance\\n  * Generates stable keys for items\\n  * Conditionally updates only when data changes\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Task 4: Update Timeline Container\\n- **Description**: Modify existing HorizontalTimelineView to integrate new scroll preservation logic\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Preserves user\'s scroll position during data refresh\\n  * No unexpected view shifts\\n  * Maintains existing functionality\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 1, Task 2, Task 3\\n- **Complexity**: Complex\\n- **Estimated Time**: 5-7 hours\\n\\n## Task 5: Implement Performance Monitoring\\n- **Description**: Add analytics and performance tracking for scroll preservation\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Tracks view stability events\\n  * Monitors render time overhead\\n  * Collects anonymous usage data for improvement\\n- **Dependencies**: Task 4\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 2-4 hours\\n\\n## Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n- **Description**: Comprehensive testing across different browsers and devices\\n- **Acceptance Criteria**:\\n  * Verified on Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\\n  * Consistent behavior on desktop and mobile\\n  * No performance regressions\\n- **Dependencies**: All previous tasks\\n- **Complexity**: Medium\\n- **Estimated Time**: 4-6 hours\\n\\n## Total Estimated Effort\\n- **Development Time**: 16-32 hours\\n- **Calendar Time**: 1-2 weeks\\n- **Complexity**: High precision refactoring\\n\\n## Recommended Implementation Order\\n1. Task 1: Scroll Position Hook\\n2. Task 2: Data Refresh Controller\\n3. Task 3: Memoized Timeline Items\\n4. Task 4: Timeline Container Update\\n5. Task 5: Performance Monitoring\\n6. Task 6: Cross-Browser Testing\\n\\n## Open Questions for Clarification\\n1. What is the acceptable performance overhead for scroll preservation?\\n2. Are there any specific browsers or devices of particular concern?\\n3. Should we implement a fallback mechanism for scroll restoration failures?"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01ShGbdPzKxcCZa9oin2Vsa9', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01ShGbdPzKxcCZa9oin2Vsa9', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Test Strategy: Timeline Page Data Refresh Focus Fix\\n\\n## Objective\\nEnsure scroll preservation in HorizontalTimelineView during data refresh, preventing user focus disruption.\\n\\n## Test Coverage Strategy\\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 90% for custom hooks and utility functions\\n- **Integration Test Coverage**: 100% for view state management\\n- **End-to-End Test Coverage**: Critical user interaction flows\\n\\n## Test Task Breakdown\\n\\n### 1. useViewState Hook Tests\\n- [ ] Verify scroll position tracking\\n- [ ] Test position preservation mechanism\\n- [ ] Validate scroll restoration functionality\\n- [ ] Check memory management and cleanup\\n\\n### 2. useDataRefresh Hook Tests\\n- [ ] Validate data refresh without view disruption\\n- [ ] Test refresh state management\\n- [ ] Verify performance during rapid successive refreshes\\n- [ ] Ensure no unexpected re-renders\\n\\n### 3. TimelineContainer Component Tests\\n- [ ] Confirm view state isolation\\n- [ ] Test integration of view state and data refresh\\n- [ ] Validate memoization effectiveness\\n- [ ] Check cross-browser scroll behavior\\n\\n### 4. Performance and Edge Case Tests\\n- [ ] Measure render time overhead\\n- [ ] Test with large datasets\\n- [ ] Validate behavior under slow network conditions\\n- [ ] Check memory usage during extended use\\n\\n### 5. End-to-End Interaction Tests\\n- [ ] Simulate real-world user scrolling during data refresh\\n- [ ] Test multiple rapid data updates\\n- [ ] Verify no unexpected view shifts\\n- [ ] Validate smooth user experience\\n\\n## Testing Tools and Frameworks\\n- **Unit Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library\\n- **Performance Testing**: React DevTools Profiler\\n- **E2E Testing**: Playwright\\n- **Scroll Simulation**: Custom scroll event generators\\n\\n## Specific Test Scenarios\\n\\n### Positive Scenarios\\n1. User scrolls midway through timeline\\n2. Data refresh occurs without changing scroll position\\n3. Multiple rapid data updates\\n4. Large dataset with continuous updates\\n\\n### Negative/Edge Scenarios\\n1. Extremely fast scroll during refresh\\n2. Refresh during scroll momentum\\n3. Low-performance devices\\n4. Interrupted network conditions\\n\\n## Performance Benchmarks\\n- **Render Time**: &lt; 5ms overhead\\n- **Memory Usage**: No significant increase\\n- **Scroll Smoothness**: 60 FPS minimum\\n\\n## Risk Mitigation Tests\\n- Verify fallback mechanisms\\n- Test feature flag integration\\n- Validate graceful degradation\\n\\n## Recommended Test Sequence\\n1. Unit tests for individual hooks\\n2. Component integration tests\\n3. Performance benchmark tests\\n4. End-to-end user flow tests\\n5. Cross-browser compatibility tests\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign testing\\n- Testing unrelated components\\n- Network layer testing beyond current implementation\\n\\n## Deliverables\\n- Comprehensive test coverage report\\n- Performance metrics documentation\\n- Recommendations for further optimization"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01158rg78fd7hHZVoeMh4VyL', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': 'ae8d6a4b', 'category': 'issue', 'note': 'Implementation appears incomplete: Only basic prop handling added to HorizontalTimelineView.jsx. Missing core scroll preservation hooks (useViewState, useDataRefresh), TimelineContainer wrapper component, and comprehensive testing. Need to complete implementation according to architecture and task specifications.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01158rg78fd7hHZVoeMh4VyL', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01SMFLuZFSjWiVTGao2AQwHt', 'name': 'spawn_agent', 'input': {'agent_type': 'coordination/frontend_coordinator', 'input_data': {'task_file': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m1.md', 'output_directory': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src', 'milestone_number': 1}}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01SMFLuZFSjWiVTGao2AQwHt', 'content': '{"success": false, "error": "Unknown agent type: coordination/frontend_coordinator. Agent definition file not found."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NzK3ne38nGcyMQ8P2a8VmE', 'name': 'run_command', 'input': {'command': 'find /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/runtime/agents -name "*frontend*" -o -name "*Frontend*"'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NzK3ne38nGcyMQ8P2a8VmE', 'content': '{"success": true, "exit_code": 0, "stdout": "", "stderr": ""}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across executions\nRecords decision history (proto-history as requested)\nTracks what\'s done vs what\'s left\nVisible in UI for user monitoring\nStored in ~/.ensemble/projects/ for persistence\n\n### Example Flow:\n\n\n**What You Write vs What Development Manager Writes:**\n**You write**: requirements.md, status reports\n**Development Manager writes**: ALL implementation code (.py, .js,